<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<usx version="2.6">
  <book code="1KI" style="id">- Tov Rose New Messianic Version Bible</book>
  <para style="h">1 Kings</para>
  <para style="mt">1 Kings</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was old <char style="add">[and]</char> stricken in years; and they covered him with clothes, but he got no heat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />For what reason his servants said unto him, Let there be sought for my lord the king a young virgin: and let her stand before the king, and let her cherish him, and let her lie in your<char style="ord">i</char> bosom, that my lord the king may get heat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />So they sought for a fair girl throughout all the coasts of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and found Avishag <char style="add">[my father is a wanderer]</char> a Shunamit <char style="add">[double resting place]</char>, and brought her to the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the girl <char style="add">[was]</char> very fair, and cherished the king, and ministered to him: but the king knew her not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> the son of Haggit <char style="add">[festive]</char> exalted himself, saying, I will be king: and he prepared him chariots and horsemen, and fifty men to run before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And his father had not displeased him at any time in saying, Why have you<char style="ord">i</char> done so? and he also <char style="add">[was a]</char> very goodly <char style="add">[man]</char>; and <char style="add">[his mother]</char> bore him after Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And he conferred with Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>, and with Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priest: and they following Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> helped <char style="add">[him]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest, and B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, and Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet, and Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char>, and Re’i <char style="add">[friendly]</char>, and the mighty men which <char style="add">[belonged]</char> to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, were not with Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> killed sheep and oxen and fat cattle by the stone of Zochelet <char style="add">[serpent]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> by ‘Ein-Rogel <char style="pn">(a place near Jerusalem)</char> <char style="add">[Fount of the Fuller (washer and/or bleacher of clothes)]</char>, and called all his brethren the king’s sons, and all the men of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> the king’s servants:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />But Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet, and B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char>, and the mighty men, and Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> his brother, he called not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For what reason Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> spoke unto Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char> the mother of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, saying, Have you<char style="ord">i</char> not heard that Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> the son of Haggit <char style="add">[festive]</char> does reign, and David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> our lord knows <char style="add">[it]</char> not?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Now therefore come, let me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, give your<char style="ord">i</char> counsel, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may save your<char style="ord">i</char> own life, and the life of your<char style="ord">i</char> son Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Go and get you<char style="ord">i</char> in unto king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and say unto him, Didst not you<char style="ord">i</char>, my lord, O king, swear unto you<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, saying, Assuredly Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne? why then does Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> reign?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Behold, while you<char style="ord">i</char> yet talk there with the king, I also will come in after you<char style="ord">i</char>, and confirm your<char style="ord">i</char> words.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char> went in unto the king into the chamber: and the king was very old; and Avishag <char style="add">[my father is a wanderer]</char> the Shunamit <char style="add">[double resting place]</char> ministered unto the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char> bowed, and did obesiance <char style="pn">(bowing or kneeling in respect)</char> unto the king. And the king said, What would you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And she said unto him, My lord, you<char style="ord">i</char> swore by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> unto your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Assuredly Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And now, behold, Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> reigns; and now, my lord the king, you<char style="ord">i</char> know <char style="add">[it]</char> not:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he has slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and has called all the sons of the king, and Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priest, and Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the captain of the host: but Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> servant has he not called.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char>, my lord, O king, the eyes of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [are]</char> upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> should tell them who shall sit on the throne of my lord the king after him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Otherwise it shall come to pass, when my lord the king shall sleep with his fathers, that I and my son Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> shall be counted offenders.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And, lo, while she yet talked with the king, Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet also came in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And they told the king, saying, Behold Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet. And when he was come in before the king, he bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> said, My lord, O king, have you<char style="ord">i</char> said, Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />For he is gone down this day, and has slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and has called all the king’s sons, and the captains of the host, and Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priest; and, behold, they eat and drink before him, and say, Long live king Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char>!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />But me, <char style="add">[even]</char> me your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest, and B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, and your<char style="ord">i</char> servant Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, has he not called.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Is this thing done by my lord the king, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have not showed <char style="add">[it]</char> unto your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, who should sit on the throne of my lord the king after him?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Then king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> answered and said, Call me Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char>. And she came into the king’s presence, and stood before the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the king swore, and said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, that has redeemed my soul out of all distress,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Even as I swore unto you<char style="ord">i</char> by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, Assuredly Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne in my stead; even so will I certainly do this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Then Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char> bowed with <char style="add">[her]</char> face to the earth, and did reverence to the king, and said, Let my lord king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> live forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> said, Call me Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest, and Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet, and B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>. And they came before the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />The king also said unto them, Take with you the servants of your lord, and cause Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> my son to ride upon my own mule, and bring him down to Gikhon <char style="pn">(Bursting Forth)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And let Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest and Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet anoint him there king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and blow you<char style="ord">2f</char> with the trumpet, and say, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> save king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />Then you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall come up after him, that he may come and sit upon my throne; for he shall be king in my stead: and I have appointed him to be ruler over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> answered the king, and said, Amen: the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of my lord the king say so <char style="add">[too]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />As the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has been with my lord the king, even so be he with Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and make his throne greater than the throne of my lord king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />So Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest, and Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet, and B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, and the K’reti <char style="add">[executioners]</char>, and the P’leti <char style="add">[couriers]</char>, went down, and caused Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> to ride upon king David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s mule, and brought him to Gikhon <char style="pn">(Bursting Forth)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest took an horn of oil out of the tabernacle, and anointed Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>. And they blew the trumpet; and all the people said, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> save king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And all the people came up after him, and the people piped with pipes, and rejoiced with great joy, so that the earth rent with the sound of them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> and all the guests that <char style="add">[were]</char> with him heard <char style="add">[it]</char> as they had made an end of eating. And when Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> heard the sound of the trumpet, he said, For what reason <char style="add">[is this]</char> noise of the city being in an uproar?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And while he yet spoke, behold, Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> the son of Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priest came: and Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> said unto him, Come in; for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a valiant man, and brings good tidings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And Y’honatan <char style="add">[Yehovah has Given]</char> answered and said to Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char>, Truly our lord king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> has made Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And the king has sent with him Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest, and Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet, and B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, and the K’reti <char style="add">[executioners]</char>, and the P’leti <char style="add">[couriers]</char>, and they have caused him to ride upon the king’s mule:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest and Natan <char style="add">[giver]</char> the prophet have anointed him king in Gikhon <char style="pn">(Bursting Forth)</char>: and they are come up from there rejoicing, so that the city rang again. This <char style="add">[is]</char> the noise that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have heard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />And also Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> sits on the throne of the kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />And moreover the king’s servants came to bless our lord king David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, saying, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> make the name of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> better than you<char style="ord">i</char> name, and make his throne greater than you<char style="ord">i</char> throne. And the king bowed himself upon the bed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And also thus said the king, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which has given <char style="add">[one]</char> to sit on my throne this day, my eyes even seeing <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />And all the guests that <char style="add">[were]</char> with Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> were afraid, and rose up, and went every man his way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />And Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> feared because of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and arose, and went, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />And it was told Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, saying, Behold, Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> fears king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>: for, lo, he has caught hold on the horns of the altar, saying, Let king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> swear unto me today that he will not slay his servant with the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> said, If he will show himself a worthy man, there shall not an hair of him fall to <char style="pn">(to do entirely, do wholly)</char> the earth: but if wickedness shall be found in him, he shall die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" />So king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> sent, and they brought him down from the altar. And he came and bowed himself to king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>: and Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> said unto him, Go to your<char style="ord">i</char> house.</para>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now the days of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> drew near that he should die; and he charged Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> his son, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />I go the way of all the earth: be you<char style="ord">i</char> strong therefore, and show yourself a man;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And keep the charge of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to walk in his ways, to keep his statutes, and his commandments, and his judgments, and his testimonies, as it is written in the law of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> may prosper in all that you<char style="ord">i</char> do, and to wherever you<char style="ord">i</char> turn yourself:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />That the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> may continue his word which he spoke concerning me, saying, If you<char style="ord">i</char> children take heed to their way, to walk before me in twith all their heart and with all their soul, there shall not fail you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="pn">(said he)</char> a man on the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Moreover you<char style="ord">i</char> know also what Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char> did to me, <char style="add">[and]</char> what he did to the two captains of the hosts of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, unto Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>, and unto ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> the son of Yeter <char style="add">[abundance]</char>, whom he killed, and shed the blood of war in peace, and put the blood of war upon his belt that <char style="add">[was]</char> about his waist, and in his shoes that <char style="add">[were]</char> on his feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Do therefore according to your<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom, and let not his grey head go down to the grave in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />But show kindness unto the sons of Barzillai <char style="add">[my iron]</char> the Gil’adi <char style="add">[Hill of Testimony]</char>, and let them be of those that eat at you<char style="ord">i</char> table: for so they came to me when I fled because of Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And, behold, <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char> have]</char> with you<char style="ord">i</char> Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> the son of Gera <char style="add">[A Grain]</char>, from the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[A Son of the Right Hand]</char> of Bachurim <char style="add">[young men’s Villiage]</char>, which cursed me with a grievous curse in the day when I went to Machanayim <char style="add">[Two Camps]</char>: but he came down to meet me at Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>, and I swore to him by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, I will not put you<char style="ord">i</char> to death with the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Now therefore hold him not guiltless: for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a wise man, and know what you<char style="ord">i</char> ought to do unto him; but his grey head bring you<char style="ord">i</char> down to the grave with blood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the days that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> reigned over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [were]</char> forty years: seven years reigned he in Hevron <char style="add">[Seat of Association]</char>, and thirty and three years reigned he in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then sat Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> upon the throne of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father; and his kingdom was established greatly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> the son of Haggit <char style="add">[festive]</char> came to Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char> the mother of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>. And she said, Come you<char style="ord">i</char> peaceably? And he said, Peaceably.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />He said moreover, I have somewhat to say unto you<char style="ord">i</char>. And she said, Say on.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he said, you<char style="ord">i</char> know that the kingdom was my, and <char style="add">[that]</char> all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> set their faces on me, that I should reign: howbeit the kingdom is turned about, and is become my brother’s: for it was his from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And now I ask one petition of you<char style="ord">i</char>, deny me not. And she said unto him, Say on.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said, Speak, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, unto Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> the king, <char style="pn">(for he will not say you<char style="ord">i</char> No,)</char> that he give me Avishag <char style="add">[my father is a wanderer]</char> the Shunamit <char style="add">[double resting place]</char> to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char> said, Well; I will speak for you<char style="ord">i</char> unto the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Bat-Sheva <char style="add">[daughter of an oath]</char> therefore went unto king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, to speak unto him for Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char>. And the king rose up to meet her, and bowed himself unto her, and sat down on his throne, and caused a seat to be set for the king’s mother; and she sat on his right hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Then she said, I desire one small petition of you<char style="ord">i</char>; <char style="add">[I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char>, say me not No. And the king said unto her, Ask on, my mother: for I will not say you<char style="ord">i</char> No.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And she said, Let Avishag <char style="add">[my father is a wanderer]</char> the Shunamit <char style="add">[double resting place]</char> be given to Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> brother to wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> answered and said unto his mother, And why do you<char style="ord">i</char> ask Avishag <char style="add">[my father is a wanderer]</char> the Shunamit <char style="add">[double resting place]</char> for Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char>? ask for him the kingdom also; for he <char style="add">[is]</char> my elder brother; even for him, and for Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priest, and for Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the son of Tz’ruyah <char style="add">[balsam]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> swore by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> do so to me, and more also, if Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> have not spoken this word against his own life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Now therefore, <char style="add">[as]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, which has established me, and set me on the throne of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, and who has made me an house, as he promised, Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char> shall be put to death this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> sent by the hand of B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>; and he fell upon him that he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And unto Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> the priest said the king, Get you<char style="ord">i</char> to ‘Anatot <char style="add">[answers to prayer]</char>, unto your<char style="ord">i</char> own fields; for you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> worthy of death: but I will not at this time put you<char style="ord">i</char> to death, because you<char style="ord">i</char> barest the ark of the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char> before David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, and because you<char style="ord">i</char> have been afflicted in all wherein my father was afflicted.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />So Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> thrust out Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char> from being priest unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; that he might fulfill the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke concerning the house of ‘Eli <char style="add">[ascension]</char> in Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Then tidings came to Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>: for Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> had turned after Adoniyah <char style="add">[my lord is Yehovah]</char>, though he turned not after Avshalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>. And Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> fled unto the tabernacle of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and caught hold on the horns of the altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And it was told king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> that Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> was fled unto the tabernacle of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; and, behold, <char style="add">[he is]</char> by the altar. Then Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> sent B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>, saying, Go, fall upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> came to the tabernacle of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said unto him, Thus says the king, Come forth. And he said, No; but I will die here. And B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> brought the king word again, saying, Thus said Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and thus he answered me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the king said unto him, Do as he has said, and fall upon him, and bury him; that you<char style="ord">i</char> may take away the innocent blood, which Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> shed, from me, and from the house of my father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall return his blood upon his own head, who fell upon two men more righteous and better than he, and killed them with the sword, my father David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> not knowing <char style="add">[thereof, that is to say]</char>, Avner <char style="add">[my father is a lamp]</char> the son of Ner <char style="add">[lamp]</char>, captain of the host of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and ‘Amasa <char style="add">[burden]</char> the son of Yeter <char style="add">[abundance]</char>, captain of the host of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Their blood shall therefore return upon the head of Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char>, and upon the head of his seed forever: but upon David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and upon his seed, and upon his house, and upon his throne, shall there be peace forever from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />So B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> went up, and fell upon him, and killed him: and he was buried in his own house in the wilderness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the king put B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char> in his room over the host: and Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest did the king put in the room of Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And the king sent and called for Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char>, and said unto him, Build you<char style="ord">i</char> an house in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and dwell there, and go not forth there any to which.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />For it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> on the day you<char style="ord">i</char> go out, and pass over the brook Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know for certain that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely die: your<char style="ord">i</char> blood shall be upon your<char style="ord">i</char> own head.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> said unto the king, The saying <char style="add">[is]</char> good: as my lord the king has said, so will your<char style="ord">i</char> servant do. And Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> dwelt in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> many days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And it came to pass at the end of three years, that two of the servants of Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> ran away unto Akhish <char style="add">[meaning disputed; I will blacken (or terrify) or only a man]</char> son of Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression]</char> king of Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>. And they told Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char>, saying, Behold, your<char style="ord">i</char> servants <char style="add">[be]</char> in Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> arose, and saddled his ass, and went to Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char> to Akhish [meaning disputed; I will blacken <char style="pn">(or terrify)</char> or only a man] to seek his servants: and Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> went, and brought his servants from Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And it was told Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> that Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> had gone from Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> to Gat <char style="add">[Winepress]</char>, and was come again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And the king sent and called for Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char>, and said unto him, Did I not make you<char style="ord">i</char> to swear by the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and protested unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Know for a certain, on the day you<char style="ord">i</char> go out, and walk abroad any to which, that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall surely die? and you<char style="ord">i</char> said unto me, The word <char style="add">[that]</char> I have heard <char style="add">[is]</char> good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />Why then have you<char style="ord">i</char> not kept the oath of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the commandment that I have charged you<char style="ord">i</char> with?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />The king said moreover to Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> know all the wickedness which your<char style="ord">i</char> heart is privy <char style="pn">(knowing a secret)</char> to, that you<char style="ord">i</char> did to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father: therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall return your<char style="ord">i</char> wickedness upon your<char style="ord">i</char> own head;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace] [shall be]</char> Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char>, and the throne of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> shall be established before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />So the king commanded B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows]</char>; which went out, and fell upon him, that he died. And the kingdom was established in the hand of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made alliance with Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and took Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> daughter, and brought her into the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, until he had made an end of building his own house, and the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the wall of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Only the people sacrificed in high places, because there was no house built unto the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, until those days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> loved the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, walking in the statutes of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father: only he sacrificed and burnt incense in high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king went to Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char> to sacrifice there; for that <char style="add">[was]</char> the great high place: a thousand burnt offerings did Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> offer upon that altar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />In Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appeared to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> in a dream by night: and God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said, Ask what I shall give you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> said, you<char style="ord">i</char> have showed unto you<char style="ord">i</char> servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father great mercy, according as he walked before you<char style="ord">i</char> in truth, and in righteousness, and in uprightness of heart with you<char style="ord">i</char>; and you<char style="ord">i</char> have kept for him this great kindness, that you<char style="ord">i</char> have given him a son to sit on his throne, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And now, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> have made you<char style="ord">i</char> servant king instead of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father: and I <char style="add">[am but]</char> a little child: I know not <char style="add">[how]</char> to go out or come in.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And your<char style="ord">i</char> servant <char style="add">[is]</char> in the midst of your<char style="ord">i</char> people which you<char style="ord">i</char> have chosen, a great people, that cannot be numbered nor counted for multitude.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Give therefore your<char style="ord">i</char> servant an understanding heart to judge your<char style="ord">i</char> people, that I may discern between good and bad: for who is able to judge this your<char style="ord">i</char> so great a people?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the speech pleased the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, that Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had asked this thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said unto him, Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have asked this thing, and have not asked for yourself long life; neither have asked riches for yourself, nor have asked the life of your<char style="ord">i</char> enemies; but have asked for yourself understanding to discern judgment;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Behold, I have done according to your<char style="ord">i</char> words: lo, I have given you<char style="ord">i</char> a wise and an understanding heart; so that there was none like you<char style="ord">i</char> before you<char style="ord">i</char>, neither after you<char style="ord">i</char> shall any arise like unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And I have also given you<char style="ord">i</char> that which you<char style="ord">i</char> have not asked, both riches, and honour: so that there shall not be any among the kings like unto you<char style="ord">i</char> all your<char style="ord">i</char> days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And if you<char style="ord">i</char> will walk in my ways, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as your<char style="ord">i</char> father David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> did walk, then I will lengthen your<char style="ord">i</char> days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> awoke; and, behold, <char style="add">[it was]</char> a dream. And he came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and stood before the ark of the covenant of the Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char>, and offered up burnt offerings, and offered peace offerings, and made a feast to all his servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Then came there two women, <char style="add">[that were]</char> prostitutes, unto the king, and stood before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the one woman said, O my lord, I and this woman dwell in one house; and I was delivered of a child with her in the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And it came to pass the third day after that I was delivered, that this woman was delivered also: and we <char style="add">[were]</char> together; <char style="add">[there was]</char> no stranger with us in the house, save we two in the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And this woman’s child died in the night; because she overlaid it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And she arose at midnight, and took my son from beside me, while your<char style="ord">i</char> female servant slept, and laid it in her bosom, and laid her dead child in my bosom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And when I rose in the morning to give my child suck, behold, it was dead: but when I had considered it in the morning, behold, it was not my son, which I did bear.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the other woman said, No; but the living <char style="add">[is]</char> my son, and the dead <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> son. And this said, No; but the dead <char style="add">[is]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> son, and the living <char style="add">[is]</char> my son. Thus they spoke before the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Then said the king, The one says, This <char style="add">[is]</char> my son that lives, and your<char style="ord">i</char> son <char style="add">[is]</char> the dead: and the other says, No; but your<char style="ord">i</char> son <char style="add">[is]</char> the dead, and my son <char style="add">[is]</char> the living.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the king said, Bring me a sword. And they brought a sword before the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the king said, Divide the living child in two, and give half to the one, and half to the other.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />Then spoke the woman whose the living child <char style="add">[was]</char> unto the king, for her bowels <char style="pn">(inward parts; affections)</char> yearned upon her son, and she said, O my lord, give her the living child, and in no way slay it. But the other said, Let it be neither my nor your<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[but]</char> divide <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Then the king answered and said, Give her the living child, and assuredly not <char style="pn">(by no means)</char> slay it: she <char style="add">[is]</char> the mother thereof.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> heard of the judgment which the king had judged; and they feared the king: for they saw that the wisdom of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [was]</char> in him, to do judgment.</para>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />So king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> was king over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[were]</char> the princes which he had; ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> the priest,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Elichoref <char style="add">[God of winter (harvest time)]</char> and Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>, the sons of Shisha <char style="add">[Yehovah contends]</char>, scribes; Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the son of Achilud <char style="add">[child’s brother]</char>, the recorder.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And B’nayahu <char style="add">[Yehovah has built]</char> the son of Y’hoyada <char style="add">[Yehovah knows] [was]</char> over the host: and Tzadok <char style="add">[righteous]</char> and Avyatar <char style="add">[my father is great] [were]</char> the priests:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And ‘Azaryah <char style="add">[Yehovah has helped]</char> the son of Natan <char style="add">[giver] [was]</char> over the officers: and Zavud <char style="add">[given]</char> the son of Natan <char style="add">[giver] [was]</char> principal officer, <char style="add">[and]</char> the king’s friend:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Achishar <char style="add">[my brother sang] [was]</char> over the household: and Adoniram <char style="add">[my lord is exalted]</char> the son of ‘Avda <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah] [was]</char> over the tribute.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had twelve officers over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which provided victuals <char style="pn">(food for humans)</char> for the king and his household: each man his month in a year made provision.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And these <char style="add">[are]</char> their names: The son of Hur <char style="add">[Liberty]</char>, in mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />The son of Deker <char style="add">[son of stabbing]</char>, in Makatz <char style="add">[end]</char>, and in Sha’alvim <char style="add">[Place of Foxes]</char>, and Beit-Shemesh <char style="add">[House of the Sun]</char>, and Eilon-Beit-Hanan <char style="add">[oak of the house of grace]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />The son of Hesed <char style="add">[son of mercy]</char>, in Arubot <char style="add">[windows]</char>; to him <char style="add">[pertained]</char> Sokhoh <char style="add">[bushy]</char>, and all the land of Hefer <char style="add">[A Well]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />The son of Avinadav <char style="add">[my father is noble]</char>, in all the region of Dor <char style="add">[Generation]</char>; which had Tafat <char style="add">[ornament]</char> the daughter of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> to wife:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Ba’ana <char style="add">[in the affliction]</char> the son of Achilud <char style="add">[child’s brother]</char>; <char style="add">[to him pertained]</char> Ta’anakh <char style="add">[Sandy]</char> and Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char>, and all Beit-Sh’an <char style="add">[House of Ease]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> by Tzartan <char style="add">[their distress]</char> beneath Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, from Beit-Sh’an <char style="add">[House of Ease]</char> to Avel-M’cholah <char style="add">[Meadow of Dancing]</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto <char style="add">[the place that is]</char> beyond Yokne’am <char style="add">[The People Lament]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />The son of Gever <char style="add">[the Son of man]</char>, in Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>; to him <char style="add">[pertained]</char> the towns of Ya’ir <char style="add">[He Enlightens]</char> the son of M’nasheh <char style="add">[Causing to Forget]</char>, which <char style="add">[are]</char> in Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>; to him <char style="add">[also pertained]</char> the region of Argov <char style="add">[Heap of Clods]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char>, threescore great cities with walls and brazen bars:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Ahinadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char> the son of ‘Iddo <char style="add">[His witness] [had]</char> Machanayim <char style="add">[Two Camps]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Achima’atz [my brother is anger (wrath)] <char style="add">[was]</char> in Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>; he also took Basmat <char style="add">[spice]</char> the daughter of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> to wife:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Ba’anah <char style="add">[in affliction]</char> the son of Hushai <char style="add">[hasting] [was]</char> in Asher <char style="add">[Happy]</char> and in Alot <char style="add">[mistresses]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the son of Paruach <char style="add">[sprout]</char>, in Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Shime’i <char style="add">[Fame]</char> the son of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char>, in Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Gever <char style="add">[the Son of man]</char> the son of Uri <char style="add">[my light, my fire] [was]</char> in the country of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, <char style="add">[in]</char> the country of Sichon <char style="add">[Warrior]</char> king of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, and of ‘Og <char style="add">[Long-necked]</char> king of Bashan <char style="add">[Fruitful]</char>; and <char style="add">[he was]</char> the only officer which <char style="add">[was]</char> in the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [were]</char> many, as the sand which <char style="add">[is]</char> by the sea in multitude, eating and drinking, and making merry.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> reigned over all kingdoms from the river unto the land of the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>, and unto the border of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>: they brought presents, and served Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> all the days of his life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> provision for one day was thirty measures of fine flour, and threescore measures of meal,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Ten fat oxen, and twenty oxen out of the pastures, and an hundred sheep, beside harts, and roebucks, and fallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> deer, and fatted fowl.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />For he had dominion over all <char style="add">[the region]</char> on this side the river, from Tifsach <char style="add">[cross over]</char> even to ‘Azah <char style="add">[The Strong]</char>, over all the kings on this side the river: and he had peace on all sides round about him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> dwelt safely, every man under his vine and under his fig tree, from Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char> even to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>, all the days of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had forty thousand stalls of horses for his chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And those officers provided victual for king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and for all that came unto king Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> table, every man in his month: they lacked nothing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Barley also and straw for the horses and dromedaries brought they unto the place where <char style="add">[the officers]</char> were, every man according to his charge.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> gave Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> wisdom and understanding exceeding much, and largeness of heart, even as the sand that <char style="add">[is]</char> on the sea shore.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> wisdom excelled the wisdom of all the children of the east country, and all the wisdom of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />For he was wiser than all men; than Eitan <char style="add">[enduring]</char> the Ezrachi <char style="add">[a native (as arising out of the soil)]</char>, and Heiman <char style="add">[faithful]</char>, and Kalkol <char style="add">[sustaining]</char>, and Darda <char style="add">[pearl of knowledge]</char>, the sons of Machol <char style="add">[dancing]</char>: and his fame was in all nations round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And he spoke three thousand proverbs: and his songs were a thousand and five.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And he spoke of trees, from the cedar tree that <char style="add">[is]</char> in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char> even unto the hyssop that springs out of the wall: he spoke also of beasts, and of fowl, and of creeping things, and of fishes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And there came of all people to hear the wisdom of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, from all kings of the earth, which had heard of his wisdom.</para>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> king of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyre)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> sent his servants unto Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>; for he had heard that they had anointed him king in the room of his father: for Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> was ever a lover of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> sent to Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />you<char style="ord">i</char> know how that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father could not build an house unto the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> for the wars which were about him on every side, until the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> put them under the soles of his feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But now the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> has given me rest on every side, <char style="add">[so that there is]</char> neither adversary nor evil evident.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And, behold, I purpose to build an house unto the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, saying, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> son, whom I will set upon your<char style="ord">i</char> throne in your<char style="ord">i</char> room, he shall build an house unto my name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Now therefore command you<char style="ord">i</char> that they hew me cedar trees out of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>; and my servants shall be with your<char style="ord">i</char> servants: and unto you<char style="ord">i</char> will I give wages for your<char style="ord">i</char> servants according to all that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall appoint: for you<char style="ord">i</char> know that <char style="add">[there is]</char> not among us any that can skill to hew timber like unto the Tzidonim <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> heard the words of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, that he rejoiced greatly, and said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> this day, which has given unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> a wise son over this great people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> sent to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, saying, I have considered the things which you<char style="ord">i</char> sent to me for: <char style="add">[and]</char> I will do all your<char style="ord">i</char> desire concerning timber of cedar, and concerning timber of fir.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />My servants shall bring <char style="add">[them]</char> down from L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char> unto the sea: and I will convey them by sea in floats unto the place that you<char style="ord">i</char> shall appoint me, and will cause them to be discharged there, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall receive <char style="add">[them]</char>: and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall accomplish my desire, in giving food for my household.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> gave Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> cedar trees and fir trees <char style="add">[according to]</char> all his desire.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> gave Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> twenty thousand measures of wheat <char style="add">[for]</char> food to his household, and twenty measures of pure oil: thus gave Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> to Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> year by year.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> gave Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> wisdom, as he promised him: and there was peace between Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> and Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>; and they two made a league (a covenant or compact made between persons, parties, states, etc., for the promotion or maintenance of common interests or for mutual assistance or service.) together.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> raised a levy out of all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and the levy was thirty thousand men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he sent them to L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, ten thousand a month by courses: a month they were in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> two months at home: and Adoniram <char style="add">[my lord is exalted] [was]</char> over the levy.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had threescore and ten thousand that bore burdens, and eighty thousand hewers in the mountains;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Beside the chief of Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> officers which <char style="add">[were]</char> over the work, three thousand and three hundred, which ruled over the people that wrought in the work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the king commanded, and they brought great stones, costly stones, <char style="add">[and]</char> hewed stones, to lay the foundation of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> builders and Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char>’s builders did hew <char style="add">[them]</char>, and the stonesquarers: so they prepared timber and stones to build the house.</para>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass in the four hundred and eightieth year after the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were come out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, in the fourth year of Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, in the month Ziv <char style="add">[brightness]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> the second month, that he began to build the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the house which king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> built for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the length thereof <char style="add">[was]</char> threescore cubits, and the breadth thereof twenty <char style="add">[cubits]</char>, and the height thereof thirty cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the porch before the temple of the house, twenty cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the length thereof, according to the breadth of the house; <char style="add">[and]</char> ten cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the breadth thereof before the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And for the house he made windows of narrow lights.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And against the wall of the house he built chambers round about, <char style="add">[against]</char> the walls of the house round about, <char style="add">[both]</char> of the temple and of the oracle: and he made chambers round about:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />The nethermost chamber <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits broad, and the middle <char style="add">[was]</char> six cubits broad, and the third <char style="add">[was]</char> seven cubits broad: for without <char style="add">[in the wall]</char> of the house he made narrowed rests round about, that <char style="add">[the beams]</char> should not be fastened in the walls of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the house, when it was in building, was built of stone made ready before it was brought there: so that there was neither hammer nor axe <char style="add">[nor]</char> any tool of iron heard in the house, while it was in building.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />The door for the middle chamber <char style="add">[was]</char> in the right side of the house: and they went up with winding stairs into the middle <char style="add">[chamber]</char>, and out of the middle into the third.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />So he built the house, and finished it; and covered the house with beams and boards of cedar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And <char style="add">[then]</char> he built chambers against all the house, five cubits high: and they rested on the house <char style="add">[with]</char> timber of cedar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Concerning]</char> this house which you<char style="ord">i</char> are in building, if you<char style="ord">i</char> will walk in my statutes, and execute my judgments, and keep all my commandments to walk in them; then will I perform my word with you<char style="ord">i</char>, which I spoke unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> father:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And I will dwell among the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and will not forsake my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />So Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> built the house, and finished it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he built the walls of the house within with boards of cedar, both the floor of the house, and the walls of the ceiling: <char style="add">[and]</char> he covered <char style="add">[them]</char> on the inside with wood, and covered the floor of the house with planks of fir.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he built twenty cubits on the sides of the house, both the floor and the walls with boards of cedar: he even built <char style="add">[them]</char> for it within, <char style="add">[even]</char> for the oracle, <char style="add">[even]</char> for the most holy <char style="add">[place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the house, that <char style="add">[is]</char>, the temple before it, was forty cubits <char style="add">[long]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the cedar of the house within <char style="add">[was]</char> carved with knops and open flowers: all <char style="add">[was]</char> cedar; there was no stone seen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the oracle he prepared in the house within, to set there the ark of the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the oracle in the forepart <char style="add">[was]</char> twenty cubits in length, and twenty cubits in breadth, and twenty cubits in the height thereof: and he overlaid it with pure gold; and <char style="add">[so]</char> covered the altar <char style="add">[which was of]</char> cedar.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />So Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> overlaid the house within with pure gold: and he made a partition by the chains of gold before the oracle; and he overlaid it with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the whole house he overlaid with gold, until he had finished all the house: also the whole altar that <char style="add">[was]</char> by the oracle he overlaid with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And within the oracle he made two k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> <char style="add">[of]</char> olive tree, <char style="add">[each]</char> ten cubits high.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And five cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the one wing of the cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>, and five cubits the other wing of the cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>: from the uttermost part of the one wing unto the uttermost part of the other <char style="add">[were]</char> ten cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And the other cherub <char style="add">[keruv] [was]</char> ten cubits: both the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> <char style="add">[were]</char> of one measure and one size.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />The height of the one cherub <char style="add">[keruv] [was]</char> ten cubits, and so <char style="add">[was it]</char> of the other cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he set the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> within the inner house: and they stretched forth the wings of the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>, so that the wing of the one touched the <char style="add">[one]</char> wall, and the wing of the other cherub <char style="add">[keruv]</char> touched the other wall; and their wings touched one another in the midst of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he overlaid the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> with gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And he carved all the walls of the house round about with carved figures of k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> and palm trees and open flowers, within and without.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the floor of the house he overlaid with gold, within and without.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And for the entering of the oracle he made doors <char style="add">[of]</char> olive tree: the lintel <char style="pn">(top of the door frame)</char> <char style="add">[and]</char> side posts <char style="add">[were]</char> a fifth part <char style="add">[of the wall]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />The two doors also <char style="add">[were of]</char> olive tree; and he carved upon them carvings of k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> and palm trees and open flowers, and overlaid <char style="add">[them]</char> with gold, and spread gold upon the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>, and upon the palm trees.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />So also made he for the door of the temple posts <char style="add">[of]</char> olive tree, a fourth part <char style="add">[of the wall]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And the two doors <char style="add">[were of]</char> fir tree: the two leaves of the one door <char style="add">[were]</char> folding, and the two leaves of the other door <char style="add">[were]</char> folding.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And he carved <char style="add">[thereon]</char> k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> and palm trees and open flowers: and covered <char style="add">[them]</char> with gold fitted upon the carved work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And he built the inner court with three rows of hewed stone, and a row of cedar beams.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />In the fourth year was the foundation of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> laid, in the month Ziv <char style="add">[brightness]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And in the eleventh year, in the month Bul [increase: produce], which <char style="add">[is]</char> the eighth month, was the house finished throughout all the parts thereof, and according to all the fashion of it. So was he seven years in building it.</para>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />But Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> was building his own house thirteen years, and he finished all his house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />He built also the house of the forest of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>; the length thereof <char style="add">[was]</char> an hundred cubits, and the breadth thereof fifty cubits, and the height thereof thirty cubits, upon four rows of cedar pillars, with cedar beams upon the pillars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And <char style="add">[it was]</char> covered with cedar above upon the beams, that <char style="add">[lay]</char> on forty five pillars, fifteen <char style="add">[in]</char> a row.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> windows <char style="add">[in]</char> three rows, and light <char style="add">[was]</char> against light <char style="add">[in]</char> three ranks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And all the doors and posts <char style="add">[were]</char> square, with the windows: and light <char style="add">[was]</char> against light <char style="add">[in]</char> three ranks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he made a porch of pillars; the length thereof <char style="add">[was]</char> fifty cubits, and the breadth thereof thirty cubits: and the porch <char style="add">[was]</char> before them: and the <char style="add">[other]</char> pillars and the thick beam <char style="add">[were]</char> before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then he made a porch for the throne where he might judge, <char style="add">[even]</char> the porch of judgment: and <char style="add">[it was]</char> covered with cedar from one side of the floor to the other.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And his house where he dwelt <char style="add">[had]</char> another court within the porch, <char style="add">[which]</char> was of the like work. Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made also an house for Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> daughter, whom he had taken <char style="add">[to wife]</char>, like unto this porch.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />All these <char style="add">[were of]</char> costly stones, according to the measures of hewed stones, sawed with saws, within and without, even from the foundation unto the coping <char style="pn">(top of a wall, sloped to drain off water)</char>, and <char style="add">[so]</char> on the outside toward the great court.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the foundation <char style="add">[was of]</char> costly stones, even great stones, stones of ten cubits, and stones of eight cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And above <char style="add">[were]</char> costly stones, after the measures of hewed stones, and cedars.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the great court round about <char style="add">[was]</char> with three rows of hewed stones, and a row of cedar beams, both for the inner court of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and for the porch of the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> sent and fetched Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> out of Tzor <char style="add">[a rock]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />He <char style="add">[was]</char> a widow’s son of the tribe of Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>, and his father <char style="add">[was]</char> a man of Tzor <char style="add">[a rock]</char>, a worker in brass: and he was filled with wisdom, and understanding, and cunning to work all works in brass. And he came to king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and wrought all his work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For he cast two pillars of brass, of eighteen cubits high apiece: and a line of twelve cubits did compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> either of them about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he made two columns <char style="add">[of]</char> molten brass, to set upon the tops of the pillars: the height of the one column <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits, and the height of the other column <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> nets of checker work, and wreaths of chain work, for the columns which <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the top of the pillars; seven for the one column, and seven for the other column.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he made the pillars, and two rows round about upon the one network, to cover the columns that <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the top, with pomegranates: and so did he for the other column.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the columns that <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the top of the pillars <char style="add">[were]</char> of lily work in the porch, four cubits.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the columns upon the two pillars <char style="add">[had pomegranates]</char> also above, over against the belly which <char style="add">[was]</char> by the network: and the pomegranates <char style="add">[were]</char> two hundred in rows round about upon the other column.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he set up the pillars in the porch of the temple: and he set up the right pillar, and called the name thereof Yakhin <char style="add">[He will establish]</char>: and he set up the left pillar, and called the name thereof Bo’az <char style="add">[a high rate of movement]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And upon the top of the pillars <char style="add">[was]</char> lily work: so was the work of the pillars finished.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he made a molten sea, ten cubits from the one brim to the other: <char style="add">[it was]</char> round all about, and his height <char style="add">[was]</char> five cubits: and a line of thirty cubits did compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> it round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And under the brim of it round about <char style="add">[there were]</char> knops compassing it, ten in a cubit, compassing the sea round about: the knops <char style="add">[were]</char> cast in two rows, when it was cast.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />It stood upon twelve oxen, three looking toward the north, and three looking toward the west, and three looking toward the south, and three looking toward the east: and the sea <char style="add">[was set]</char> above upon them, and all their hinder parts <char style="add">[were]</char> inward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And it <char style="add">[was]</char> an hand breadth thick, and the brim thereof was wrought like the brim of a cup, with flowers of lilies: it contained two thousand baths.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he made ten bases of brass; four cubits <char style="add">[was]</char> the length of one base, and four cubits the breadth thereof, and three cubits the height of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the work of the bases <char style="add">[was]</char> on this <char style="add">[manner]</char>: they had borders, and the borders <char style="add">[were]</char> between the ledges:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And on the borders that <char style="add">[were]</char> between the ledges <char style="add">[were]</char> lions, oxen, and k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>: and upon the ledges <char style="add">[there was]</char> a base above: and beneath the lions and oxen <char style="add">[were]</char> certain additions made of thin work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And every base had four brazen wheels, and plates of brass: and the four corners thereof had supports: under the Wash basin <char style="add">[were]</char> supports molten, at the side of every addition.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And the mouth of it within the column and above <char style="add">[was]</char> a cubit: but the mouth thereof <char style="add">[was]</char> round <char style="add">[after]</char> the work of the base, a cubit and an half: and also upon the mouth of it <char style="add">[were]</char> gravings with their borders, Foursquare <char style="pn">(squared; four cornered)</char>, not round.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And under the borders <char style="add">[were]</char> four wheels; and the axletrees of the wheels <char style="add">[were joined]</char> to the base: and the height of a wheel <char style="add">[was]</char> a cubit and half a cubit.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And the work of the wheels <char style="add">[was]</char> like the work of a chariot wheel: their axletrees, and their naves, and their felloes, and their spokes, <char style="add">[were]</char> all molten.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And <char style="add">[there were]</char> four supports to the four corners of one base: <char style="add">[and]</char> the supports <char style="add">[were]</char> of the very base itself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And in the top of the base <char style="add">[was there]</char> a round compass <char style="pn">(go around, encircle; encompass)</char> of half a cubit high: and on the top of the base the ledges thereof and the borders thereof <char style="add">[were]</char> of the same.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />For on the plates of the ledges thereof, and on the borders thereof, he graved k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>, lions, and palm trees, according to the proportion of everyone, and additions round about.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />After this <char style="add">[manner]</char> he made the ten bases: all of them had one casting, one measure, <char style="add">[and]</char> one size.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />Then made he ten lavers of brass: one Wash basin contained forty baths: <char style="add">[and]</char> every Wash basin was four cubits: <char style="add">[and]</char> upon everyone of the ten bases one Wash basin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And he put five bases on the right side of the house, and five on the left side of the house: and he set the sea on the right side of the house eastward over against the south.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> made the lavers, and the shovels, and the basins. So Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> made an end of doing all the work that he made king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />The two pillars, and the <char style="add">[two]</char> bowls of the columns that <char style="add">[were]</char> on the top of the two pillars; and the two networks, to cover the two bowls of the columns which <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the top of the pillars;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And four hundred pomegranates for the two networks, <char style="add">[even]</char> two rows of pomegranates for one network, to cover the two bowls of the columns that <char style="add">[were]</char> upon the pillars;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And the ten bases, and ten lavers on the bases;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And one sea, and twelve oxen under the sea;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And the pots, and the shovels, and the basins: and all these vessels, which Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> made to king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[were of]</char> bright brass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />In the plain of Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char> did the king cast them, in the clay ground between Sukkot <char style="add">[Booths]</char> and Tzartan <char style="add">[their distress]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> left all the vessels <char style="add">[unweighed]</char>, because they were exceeding many: neither was the weight of the brass found out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made all the vessels that <char style="add">[pertained]</char> unto the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: the altar of gold, and the table of gold, whereupon the showbread <char style="add">[was]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />And the candlesticks of pure gold, five on the right <char style="add">[side]</char>, and five on the left, before the oracle, with the flowers, and the lamps, and the tongs <char style="add">[of]</char> gold,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />And the bowls, and the snuffers, and the basins, and the spoons, and the censers <char style="add">[of]</char> pure gold; and the hinges <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, <char style="add">[both]</char> for the doors of the inner house, the most holy <char style="add">[place, and]</char> for the doors of the house, <char style="add">[that is to say]</char>, of the temple.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />So was ended all the work that king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> brought in the things which David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father had dedicated; <char style="add">[even]</char> the silver, and the gold, and the vessels, did he put among the treasures of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> assembled the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and all the heads of the tribes, the chief of the fathers of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, unto king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, that they might bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> out of the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> Tziyon <char style="add">[parched place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And all the men of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> assembled themselves unto king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> at the feast in the month Etanim <char style="add">[enduring]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> the seventh month.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And all the elders of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came, and the priests took up the ark.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And they brought up the ark of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the tabernacle of the congregation, and all the holy vessels that <char style="add">[were]</char> in the tabernacle, even those did the priests and the Levi’im <char style="pn">(Levites)</char> <char style="add">[Joined to]</char> bring up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that were assembled unto him, <char style="add">[were]</char> with him before the ark, sacrificing sheep and oxen, that could not be told nor numbered for multitude.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the priests brought in the ark of the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto his place, into the oracle of the house, to the most holy <char style="add">[place, even]</char> under the wings of the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />For the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> spread forth <char style="add">[their]</char> two wings over the place of the ark, and the k’vurim <char style="pn">(cherubim)</char> covered the ark and the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> thereof above.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And they drew out the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char>, that the ends of the rods <char style="pn">(clubs)</char> were seen out in the holy <char style="add">[place]</char> before the oracle, and they were not seen without: and there they are unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There was]</char> nothing in the ark save the two tables of stone, which Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> put there at Horev <char style="add">[Desert]</char>, when the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> made <char style="add">[a covenant]</char> with the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when they came out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the priests were come out of the holy <char style="add">[place]</char>, that the cloud filled the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />So that the priests could not stand to minister because of the cloud: for the glory of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had filled the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Then spoke Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said that he would dwell in the thick darkness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />I have surely built you<char style="ord">i</char> an house to dwell in, a settled place for you<char style="ord">i</char> to abide in forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the king turned his face about, and Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> (and all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> stood;)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he said, Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which spoke with his mouth unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, and has with his hand fulfilled <char style="add">[it]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />Since the day that I brought forth my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, I chose no city out of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to build an house, that my name might be in it; but I chose David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> to be over my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it was in the heart of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father to build an house for the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, Whereas it was in you<char style="ord">i</char> heart to build an house unto my name, you<char style="ord">i</char> did well that it was in you<char style="ord">i</char> heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Nevertheless you<char style="ord">i</char> shall not build the house; but your<char style="ord">i</char> son that shall come forth out of your<char style="ord">i</char> waist, he shall build the house unto my name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has performed his word that he spoke, and I am risen up in the room of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father, and sit on the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, as the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> promised, and have built an house for the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And I have set there a place for the ark, wherein <char style="add">[is]</char> the covenant of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he made with our fathers, when he brought them out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> stood before the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in the presence of all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and spread forth his hands toward heaven:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And he said, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[there is]</char> no God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> like you<char style="ord">i</char>, in heaven above, or on earth beneath, who keeps covenant and mercy with you<char style="ord">i</char> servants that walk before you<char style="ord">i</char> with all their heart:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Who have kept with your<char style="ord">i</char> servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father that you<char style="ord">i</char> promised him: you<char style="ord">i</char> spoke also with your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth, and have fulfilled <char style="add">[it]</char> with your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, as <char style="add">[it is]</char> this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Therefore now, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, keep with your<char style="ord">i</char> servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father that you<char style="ord">i</char> promised him, saying, There shall not fail you<char style="ord">i</char> a man in my sight to sit on the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; so that your<char style="ord">i</char> children take heed to their way, that they walk before me as you<char style="ord">i</char> have walked before me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And now, O God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, let you<char style="ord">i</char> word, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, be verified, which you<char style="ord">i</char> spoke unto your<char style="ord">i</char> servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />But will God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> indeed dwell on the earth? behold, the heaven and heaven of heavens cannot contain you<char style="ord">i</char>; how much less this house that I have built?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Yet have you<char style="ord">i</char> respect unto the prayer of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and to his supplication, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to hearken unto the cry and to the prayer, which your<char style="ord">i</char> servant prays before you<char style="ord">i</char> today:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />That your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes may be open toward this house night and day, <char style="add">[even]</char> toward the place of which you<char style="ord">i</char> have said, My name shall be there: that you<char style="ord">i</char> may hearken unto the prayer which your<char style="ord">i</char> servant shall make toward this place.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And hearken you<char style="ord">i</char> to the supplication of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, when they shall pray toward this place: and hear you<char style="ord">i</char> in heaven your<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling place: and when you<char style="ord">i</char> hear, forgive.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />If any man trespass against his neighbour, and an oath be laid upon him to cause him to swear, and the oath come before your<char style="ord">i</char> altar in this house:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> in heaven, and do, and judge your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, condemning the wicked, to bring his way upon his head; and justifying the righteous, to give him according to his righteousness.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />When your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> be smitten down before the enemy, because they have sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and shall turn again to you<char style="ord">i</char>, and confess your<char style="ord">i</char> name, and pray, and make supplication unto you<char style="ord">i</char> in this house:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> in heaven, and forgive the sin of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and bring them again unto the land which you<char style="ord">i</char> gave unto their fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />When heaven is shut up, and there is no rain, because they have sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>; if they pray toward this place, and confess your<char style="ord">i</char> name, and turn from their sin, when you<char style="ord">i</char> afflict them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> in heaven, and forgive the sin of your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, and of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that you<char style="ord">i</char> teach them the good way wherein they should walk, and give rain upon your<char style="ord">i</char> land, which you<char style="ord">i</char> have given to your<char style="ord">i</char> people for an inheritance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />If there be in the land famine, if there be pestilence, blasting, mildew, locust, <char style="add">[or]</char> if there be caterpillar; if their enemy besiege them in the land of their cities; whatsoever plague, whatsoever sickness <char style="add">[there be]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />What prayer and supplication soever be <char style="add">[made]</char> by any man, <char style="add">[or]</char> by all your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which shall know every man the plague of his own heart, and spread forth his hands toward this house:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> in heaven your<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling place, and forgive, and do, and give to every man according to his ways, whose heart you<char style="ord">i</char> know; (for you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> only, know the hearts of all the children of men;)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />That they may fear you<char style="ord">i</char> all the days that they live in the land which you<char style="ord">i</char> gave unto our fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />Moreover concerning a stranger, that <char style="add">[is]</char> not of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, but comes out of a far country for your<char style="ord">i</char> name’s sake;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />(For they shall hear of your<char style="ord">i</char> great name, and of you<char style="ord">i</char> strong hand, and of your<char style="ord">i</char> stretched out arm;) when he shall come and pray toward this house;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />Hear you<char style="ord">i</char> in heaven your<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling place, and do according to all that the stranger calls to you<char style="ord">i</char> for: that all people of the earth may know your<char style="ord">i</char> name, to fear you<char style="ord">i</char>, as <char style="add">[do]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and that they may know that this house, which I have built, is called by your<char style="ord">i</char> name.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />If your<char style="ord">i</char> people go out to battle against their enemy, to wherever you<char style="ord">i</char> shall send them, and shall pray unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> toward the city which you<char style="ord">i</char> have chosen, and <char style="add">[toward]</char> the house that I have built for your<char style="ord">i</char> name:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> in heaven their prayer and their supplication, and maintain their cause.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />If they sin against you<char style="ord">i</char>, (for <char style="add">[there is]</char> no man that sins not,) and you<char style="ord">i</char> be angry with them, and deliver them to the enemy, so that they carry them away captives unto the land of the enemy, far or near;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[Yet]</char> if they shall consider themselves in the land to which they were carried captives, and repent, and make supplication unto you<char style="ord">i</char> in the land of them that carried them captives, saying, We have sinned, and have done perversely, we have committed wickedness;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />And <char style="add">[so]</char> return unto you<char style="ord">i</char> with all their heart, and with all their soul, in the land of their enemies, which led them away captive, and pray unto you<char style="ord">i</char> toward their land, which you<char style="ord">i</char> gave unto their fathers, the city which you<char style="ord">i</char> have chosen, and the house which I have built for your<char style="ord">i</char> name:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />Then hear you<char style="ord">i</char> their prayer and their supplication in heaven your<char style="ord">i</char> dwelling place, and maintain their cause,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />And forgive your<char style="ord">i</char> people that have sinned against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and all their transgressions wherein they have transgressed against you<char style="ord">i</char>, and give them compassion before them who carried them captive, that they may have compassion on them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />For they <char style="add">[be]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> people, and your<char style="ord">i</char> inheritance, which you<char style="ord">i</char> brought forth out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, from the midst of the furnace of iron:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" />That your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes may be open unto the supplication of your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and unto the supplication of your<char style="ord">i</char> people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to hearken unto them in all that they call for unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" />For you<char style="ord">i</char> did separate them from among all the people of the earth, <char style="add">[to be]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> inheritance, as you<char style="ord">i</char> spoke by the hand of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, when you<char style="ord">i</char> brought our fathers out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, O Lord-Adonai <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> GOD-Yehōvih <char style="pn">(THE FATHER)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="54" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, that when Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had made an end of praying all this prayer and supplication unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, he arose from before the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, from kneeling on his knees with his hands spread up to heaven.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="55" style="v" />And he stood, and Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with a loud voice, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="56" style="v" />Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that has given rest unto his people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, according to all that he promised: there has not failed one word of all his good promise, which he promised by the hand of Moshe <char style="add">[He Who Draws Out Of The Waters]</char> his servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="57" style="v" />The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> be with us, as he was with our fathers: let him not leave us, nor forsake us:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="58" style="v" />That he may incline our hearts unto him, to walk in all his ways, and to keep his commandments, and his statutes, and his judgments, which he commanded our fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="59" style="v" />And let these my words, which I have made supplication before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, be near unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> day and night, that he maintain the cause of his servant, and the cause of his people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> at all times, as the matter shall require:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="60" style="v" />That all the people of the earth may know that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[and that there is]</char> none else.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="61" style="v" />Let your heart therefore be perfect with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, to walk in his statutes, and to keep his commandments, as at this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="62" style="v" />And the king, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with him, offered sacrifice before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="63" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> offered a sacrifice of peace offerings, which he offered unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, two and twenty thousand oxen, and an hundred and twenty thousand sheep. So the king and all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> dedicated the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="64" style="v" />The same day did the king hallow <char style="pn">(to approve, commend, accept)</char> the middle of the court that <char style="add">[was]</char> before the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for there he offered burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings: because the brazen altar that <char style="add">[was]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> too little to receive the burnt offerings, and meat offerings, and the fat of the peace offerings.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="65" style="v" />And at that time Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> held a feast, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with him, a great congregation, from the entering in of Hamat <char style="add">[Fortress]</char> unto the river of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> our God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, seven days and seven days, <char style="add">[even]</char> fourteen days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="66" style="v" />On the eighth day he sent the people away: and they Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> the king, and went unto their tents joyful and glad of heart for all the goodness that the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> had done for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his servant, and for Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> his people.</para>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had finished the building of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the king’s house, and all Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> desire which he was pleased to do,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />That the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> appeared to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> the second time, as he had appeared unto him at Giv’on <char style="add">[Hill City]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, I have heard your<char style="ord">i</char> prayer and your<char style="ord">i</char> supplication, that you<char style="ord">i</char> have made before me: I have consecrated this house, which you<char style="ord">i</char> have built, to put my name there forever; and my eyes and my heart shall be there perpetually.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And if you<char style="ord">i</char> will walk before me, as David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> father walked, in integrity of heart, and in uprightness, to do according to all that I have commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> will keep my statutes and my judgments:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Then I will establish the throne of your<char style="ord">i</char> kingdom upon Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> forever, as I promised to David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> father, saying, There shall not fail you<char style="ord">i</char> a man upon the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[But]</char> if you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall at all turn from following me, you<char style="ord">2f</char> or your children, and will not keep my commandments <char style="add">[and]</char> my statutes which I have set before you, but go and serve other gods, and worship them:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then will I cut off Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of the land which I have given them; and this house, which I have consecrated for my name, will I cast out of my sight; and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall be a proverb and a byword among all people:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And at this house, <char style="add">[which]</char> is high, everyone that passes by it shall be astonished, and shall hiss; and they shall say, Why has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> done thus unto this land, and to this house?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And they shall answer, Because they forsook the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> their God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, who brought forth their fathers out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and have taken hold upon other gods, and have worshipped them, and served them: therefore has the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> brought upon them all this evil.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And it came to pass at the end of twenty years, when Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had built the two houses, the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the king’s house,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />(<char style="add">[Now]</char> Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> the king of Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyre)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> had furnished Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> with cedar trees and fir trees, and with gold, according to all his desire,) that then king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> gave Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> twenty cities in the land of Galil <char style="add">[circuit, district]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> came out from Tzor <char style="pn">(Tyre)</char> <char style="add">[a rock]</char> to see the cities which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had given him; and they pleased him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he said, What cities <char style="add">[are]</char> these which you<char style="ord">i</char> have given me, my brother? And he called them the land of Kavul <char style="add">[binding]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> sent to the king four tons of gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And this <char style="add">[is]</char> the reason of the levy which king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> raised; for to build the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and his own house, and Millo <char style="add">[fortification (defensive structure) or mound]</char>, and the wall of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and Hatzor <char style="add">[Castle]</char>, and Megiddo <char style="add">[Place of Crowds]</char>, and Gezer <char style="add">[Portion]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[For]</char> Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> had gone up, and taken Gezer <char style="add">[Portion]</char>, and burnt it with fire, and slain the Kena’ani <char style="add">[Merchant]</char> that dwelt in the city, and given it <char style="add">[for]</char> a present unto his daughter, Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> wife.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> built Gezer <char style="add">[Portion]</char>, and Beit-Horon <char style="add">[House of Hollowness]</char> the lower,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And Ba’alat <char style="add">[mistress]</char>, and Tadmor <char style="add">[palm tree]</char> in the wilderness, in the land,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And all the cities of store that Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had, and cities for his chariots, and cities for his horsemen, and that which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> desired to build in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and in L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>, and in all the land of his dominion.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> all the people <char style="add">[that were]</char> left of the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, P’rizi <char style="add">[Dwellers in Unwalled Towns]</char>, Hivi <char style="add">[Villagers]</char>, and Y’vusi <char style="add">[Threshers, Trampled Under Foot]</char>, which <char style="add">[were]</char> not of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Their children that were left after them in the land, whom the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> also were not able utterly to destroy, upon those did Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> levy a tribute of bond service unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But of the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> did Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> make no bondmen: but they <char style="add">[were]</char> men of war, and his servants, and his princes, and his captains, and rulers of his chariots, and his horsemen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />These <char style="add">[were]</char> the chief of the officers that <char style="add">[were]</char> over Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> work, five hundred and fifty, which bore rule over the people that wrought in the work.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />But Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> daughter came up out of the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> unto her house which <char style="add">[Shlomo (Solomon) [peace]]</char> had built for her: then did he build Millo <char style="add">[fortification (defensive structure) or mound]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And three times in a year did Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> offer burnt offerings and peace offerings upon the altar which he built unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and he burnt incense upon the altar that <char style="add">[was]</char> before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. So he finished the house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made a navy of ships in ‘Etzyon-Gever <char style="add">[backbone of a man]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> beside Elot <char style="add">[grove of lofty trees]</char>, on the shore of the Red sea, in the land of Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char> sent in the navy his servants, shipmen that had knowledge of the sea, with the servants of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And they came to Ofir <char style="add">[reducing to ashes]</char>, and fetched from there gold, four hundred and twenty talents, and brought <char style="add">[it]</char> to king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And when the Queen of Sh’va <char style="add">[seven, an oath]</char> heard of the fame of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> concerning the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, she came to prove him with hard questions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And she came to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> with a very great train, with camels that bore spices, and very much gold, and precious stones: and when she was come to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> told her all her questions: there was not <char style="add">[any]</char> thing hid from the king, which he told her not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And when the Queen of Sh’va <char style="add">[seven, an oath]</char> had seen all Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> wisdom, and the house that he had built,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel, and his cupbearers, and his ascent by which he went up unto the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; there was no more spirit in her.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And she said to the king, It was a true report that I heard in my own land of your<char style="ord">i</char> acts and of your<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />However I believed not the words, until I came, and my eyes had seen <char style="add">[it]</char>: and, behold, the half was not told me: you<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom and prosperity exceeds the fame which I heard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />Happy <char style="add">[are]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> men, happy <char style="add">[are]</char> these your<char style="ord">i</char> servants, which stand continually before you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> that hear your<char style="ord">i</char> wisdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Blessed <char style="pn">(Favored by God; happy; prosperous)</char> be the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which delighted in you<char style="ord">i</char>, to set you<char style="ord">i</char> on the throne of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: because the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> loved Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> forever, therefore made he you<char style="ord">i</char> king, to do judgment and justice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And she gave the king an hundred and twenty tons of gold, and of spices very great store, and precious stones: there came no more such abundance of spices as these which the Queen of Sh’va <char style="add">[seven, an oath]</char> gave to king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the navy also of Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char>, that brought gold from Ofir <char style="add">[reducing to ashes]</char>, brought in from Ofir <char style="add">[reducing to ashes]</char> great plenty of almug trees, and precious stones.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And the king made of the almug trees pillars for the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and for the king’s house, harps also and psalteries for singers: there came no such almug trees, nor were seen unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> gave unto the Queen of Sh’va <char style="add">[seven, an oath]</char> all her desire, whatsoever she asked, beside <char style="add">[that]</char> which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> gave her of his royal bounty. So she turned and went to her own country, she and her servants.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Now the weight of gold that came to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> in one year was six hundred threescore and six tons of gold,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Beside <char style="add">[that he had]</char> of the merchantmen, and of the traffick <char style="pn">(trade; do business)</char> of the spice merchants, and of all the kings of Arabia <char style="add">[steppe-dwellers]</char>, and of the governors of the country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> made two hundred targets <char style="add">[of]</char> beaten gold: six hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of gold went to one target <char style="pn">(small shield; buckler)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And <char style="add">[he made]</char> three hundred shields <char style="add">[of]</char> beaten gold; three pound of gold went to one shield: and the king put them in the house of the forest of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Moreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with the best gold.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />The throne had six steps, and the top of the throne <char style="add">[was]</char> round behind: and <char style="add">[there were]</char> stays on either side on the place of the seat, and two lions stood beside the stays.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other upon the six steps: there was not the like made in any kingdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And all king Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> drinking vessels <char style="add">[were of]</char> gold, and all the vessels of the house of the forest of L’vanon <char style="add">[Whiteness] [were of]</char> pure gold; none <char style="add">[were of]</char> silver: it was nothing accounted of in the days of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />For the king had at sea a navy of Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char> with the navy of Hiram <char style="add">[noble]</char>: once in three years came the navy of Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char>, bringing gold, and silver, ivory, and apes, and peacocks.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />So king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> exceeded all the kings of the earth for riches and for wisdom.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And all the earth sought to Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, to hear his wisdom, which God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had put in his heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And they brought every man his present, vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and garments, and armour, and spices, horses, and mules, a rate year by year.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> gathered together chariots and horsemen: and he had a thousand and four hundred chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen, whom he bestowed in the cities for chariots, and with the king at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the king made silver <char style="add">[to be]</char> in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> as stones, and cedars made he <char style="add">[to be]</char> as the sycamore trees that <char style="add">[are]</char> in the vale, for abundance.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had horses brought out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and linen yarn: the king’s merchants received the linen yarn at a price.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And a chariot came up and went out of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> for six hundred <char style="add">[shekels]</char> of silver, and an horse for an hundred and fifty: and so for all the kings of the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>, and for the kings of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, did they bring <char style="add">[them]</char> out by their means.</para>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />But king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> loved many strange women, together with the daughter of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, women of the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char>, <char style="add">[what father?]</char> ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char>, people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Of the nations <char style="add">[concerning]</char> which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not go in to them, neither shall they come in unto you: <char style="add">[for]</char> surely they will turn away your heart after their gods: Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> clave unto these in love.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he had seven hundred wives, princesses, and three hundred concubines: and his wives turned away his heart.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />For it came to pass, when Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> was old, <char style="add">[that]</char> his wives turned away his heart after other gods: and his heart was not perfect with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, as <char style="add">[was]</char> the heart of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />For Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> went after ‘Ashtoret <char style="add">[star]</char> the goddess of the people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and after Milkom <char style="add">[great king]</char> the abomination of the ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and went not fully after the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as <char style="add">[did]</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then did Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> build an high place for K’mosh <char style="add">[Subduer]</char>, the abomination of Mo’av <char style="add">[Seed of my Father]</char>, in the hill that <char style="add">[is]</char> before Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, and for Molekh <char style="add">[king]</char>, the abomination of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And likewise did he for all his strange wives, which burnt incense and sacrificed unto their gods.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was angry with Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, because his heart was turned from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which had appeared unto him twice,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And had commanded him concerning this thing, that he should not go after other gods: but he kept not that which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> commanded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />For what reason the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, Forasmuch as this is done of you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have not kept my covenant and my statutes, which I have commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>, I will surely rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> the kingdom from you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will give it to your<char style="ord">i</char> servant.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Yet in your<char style="ord">i</char> days I will not do it for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> father’s sake: <char style="add">[but]</char> I will rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> it out of the hand of your<char style="ord">i</char> son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />However I will not rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> away all the kingdom; <char style="add">[but]</char> will give one tribe to you<char style="ord">i</char> son for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my servant’s sake, and for Yerushalayim’s <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> sake which I have chosen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> stirred up an adversary unto Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, Hadad <char style="add">[mighty]</char> the Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char>: he <char style="add">[was]</char> of the king’s seed in Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For it came to pass, when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> was in Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>, and Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the captain of the host was gone up to bury the slain, after he had smitten every male in Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />(For six months did Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> remain there with all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, until he had cut off every male in Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />That Hadad <char style="add">[mighty]</char> fled, he and certain Edomi <char style="add">[red]</char> of his father’s servants with him, to go into Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; Hadad <char style="add">[mighty] [being]</char> yet a little child.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And they arose out of Midyan <char style="add">[Strife]</char>, and came to Pa’ran <char style="add">[place of caverns]</char>: and they took men with them out of Pa’ran <char style="add">[place of caverns]</char>, and they came to Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, unto Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>; which gave him an house, and appointed him victuals <char style="pn">(food for humans)</char>, and gave him land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And Hadad <char style="add">[mighty]</char> found great favour in the sight of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, so that he gave him to wife the sister of his own wife, the sister of Tachp’neis <char style="add">[wife of the king]</char> the queen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the sister of Tachp’neis <char style="add">[wife of the king]</char> bore him G’nuvat <char style="add">[theft]</char> his son, whom Tachp’neis <char style="add">[wife of the king]</char> weaned in Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> house: and G’nuvat <char style="add">[theft]</char> was in Par’oh’s <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> household among the sons of Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And when Hadad <char style="add">[mighty]</char> heard in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> slept with his fathers, and that Yo’av <char style="add">[Yehovah is father]</char> the captain of the host was dead, Hadad <char style="add">[mighty]</char> said to Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char>, Let me depart, that I may go to my own country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then Par’oh <char style="add">[Pharaoh - Great House]</char> said unto him, But what have you<char style="ord">i</char> lacked with me, that, behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> seek to go to your<char style="ord">i</char> own country? And he answered, Nothing: howbeit let me go in any wise.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> stirred him up <char style="add">[another]</char> adversary, Rezon <char style="add">[prince]</char> the son of Elyada <char style="add">[God knows]</char>, which fled from his lord Hadad’ezer <char style="add">[mighty - meaning disputed]</char> king of Tzovah <char style="add">[station]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he gathered men unto him, and became captain over a band, when David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> killed them <char style="add">[of Tzovah [station]]</char>: and they went to Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, and dwelt in it, and reigned in Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And he was an adversary to Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> all the days of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, beside the mischief that Hadad <char style="add">[mighty] [did]</char>: and he abhorred Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and reigned over Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, an Efrat <char style="add">[ashiness: fruitfulness]</char> of Zereda, Shlomo’s <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> servant, whose mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Tz’ru’ah <char style="add">[full breasted]</char>, a widow woman, even he lifted up <char style="add">[his]</char> hand against the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And this <char style="add">[was]</char> the cause that he lifted up <char style="add">[his]</char> hand against the king: Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> built Millo <char style="add">[fortification (defensive structure) or mound]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> repaired the breaches of the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the man Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend] [was]</char> a mighty man of valour: and Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> seeing the young man that he was industrious, he made him ruler over all the charge of the house of Yosef <char style="add">[(God) He Shall Add]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And it came to pass at that time when Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> went out of Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, that the prophet Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> the Shiloni <char style="add">[peace bringer] [place of rest]</char> found him in the way; and he had clad himself with a new garment; and they two <char style="add">[were]</char> alone in the field:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> caught the new garment that <char style="add">[was]</char> on him, and rent it <char style="add">[in]</char> twelve pieces:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And he said to Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, Take you<char style="ord">i</char> ten pieces: for thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Behold, I will rend <char style="pn">(tear apart; forcefully rip apart)</char> the kingdom out of the hand of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and will give ten tribes to you<char style="ord">i</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />(But he shall have one tribe for my servant David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s sake, and for Yerushalayim’s <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> sake, the city which I have chosen out of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Because that they have forsaken me, and have worshipped ‘Ashtoret <char style="add">[star]</char> the goddess of the people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, K’mosh <char style="add">[Subduer]</char> the god of the Mo’avi <char style="add">[of his father]</char>, and Milkom <char style="add">[great king]</char> the god of the children of ‘Amon <char style="add">[Inbred]</char>, and have not walked in my ways, to do <char style="add">[that which is]</char> right in my eyes, and <char style="add">[to keep]</char> my statutes and my judgments, as <char style="add">[did]</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />However I will not take the whole kingdom out of his hand: but I will make him prince all the days of his life for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my servant’s sake, whom I chose, because he kept my commandments and my statutes:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />But I will take the kingdom out of his son’s hand, and will give it unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[even]</char> ten tribes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And unto his son will I give one tribe, that David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my servant may have a light always before me in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, the city which I have chosen me to put my name there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />And I will take you<char style="ord">i</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall reign according to all that your<char style="ord">i</char> soul desires, and shall be king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And it shall be, if you<char style="ord">i</char> will hearken unto all that I command you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will walk in my ways, and do <char style="add">[that is]</char> right in my sight, to keep my statutes and my commandments, as David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> my servant did; that I will be with you<char style="ord">i</char>, and build you<char style="ord">i</char> a sure house, as I built for David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and will give Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And I will for this afflict the seed of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, but not forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> sought therefore to kill Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>. And Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> arose, and fled into Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, unto Shishak <char style="add">[greedy of fine linen]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, and was in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> until the death of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and all that he did, and his wisdom, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the acts of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And the time that Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> reigned in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char> over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [was]</char> forty years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father: and Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> went to Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char>: for all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were come to Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> to make him king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who was yet in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>, heard <char style="add">[of it]</char>, (for he was fled from the presence of king Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> dwelt in Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>;)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />That they sent and called him. And Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> and all the congregation of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> came, and spoke unto Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> father made our yoke grievous: now therefore make you<char style="ord">i</char> the grievous service of your<char style="ord">i</char> father, and his heavy yoke which he put upon us, lighter, and we will serve you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And he said unto them, Depart yet <char style="add">[for]</char> three days, then come again to me. And the people departed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> consulted with the old men, that stood before Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> his father while he yet lived, and said, How do you<char style="ord">2f</char> advise that I may answer this people?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And they spoke unto him, saying, If you<char style="ord">i</char> will be a servant unto this people this day, and will serve them, and answer them, and speak good words to them, then they will be your<char style="ord">i</char> servants forever.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />But he forsook the counsel of the old men, which they had given him, and consulted with the young men that were grown up with him, <char style="add">[and]</char> which stood before him:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he said unto them, What counsel give you<char style="ord">2f</char> that we may answer this people, who have spoken to me, saying, Make the yoke which your<char style="ord">i</char> father did put upon us lighter?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the young men that were grown up with him spoke unto him, saying, Thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> speak unto this people that spoke unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> father made our yoke heavy, but make you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[it]</char> lighter unto us; thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto them, My little <char style="add">[finger]</char> shall be thicker than my father’s waist <char style="pn">(hips)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And now whereas my father did burden <char style="pn">(to load)</char> you with a heavy yoke, I will add to your yoke: my father has chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />So Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> and all the people came to Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> the third day, as the king had appointed, saying, Come to me again the third day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the king answered the people roughly, and forsook the old men’s counsel that they gave him;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And spoke to them after the counsel of the young men, saying, My father made your yoke heavy, and I will add to your yoke: my father <char style="add">[also]</char> chastised you with whips, but I will chastise you with scorpions.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For what reason the king listened not unto the people; for the cause was from the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that he might perform his saying, which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> spoke by Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> the Shiloni <char style="add">[peace bringer] [place of rest]</char> unto Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />So when all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> saw that the king listened not unto them, the people answered the king, saying, What portion have we in David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>? neither <char style="add">[have we]</char> inheritance in the son of Yishai <char style="add">[I possess]</char>: to your tents, O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: now see to your<char style="ord">i</char> own house, David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. So Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> departed unto their tents.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />But <char style="add">[as for]</char> the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> which dwelt in the cities of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> reigned over them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> sent Adoram <char style="add">[my lord is exalted]</char>, who <char style="add">[was]</char> over the tribute; and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> stoned him with stones, that he died. Therefore king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> made speed to get him up to his chariot, to flee to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />So Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> rebelled against the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> unto this day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And it came to pass, when all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> heard that Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> was come again, that they sent and called him unto the congregation, and made him king over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: there was none that followed the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, but the tribe of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> only.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And when Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> was come to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, he assembled all the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, with the tribe of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, an hundred and eighty thousand chosen men, which were warriors, to fight against the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to bring the kingdom again to Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> the son of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But the word of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> came unto Sh’may’yah <char style="add">[Yehovah hears]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Speak unto Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char>, the son of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char>, king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and unto all the house of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> and Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and to the remnant of the people, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, You<char style="ord">2f</char> shall not go up, nor fight against your brethren the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: return every man to his house; for this thing is from me. They listened therefore to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and returned to depart, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />Then Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> built Sh’khem <char style="add">[Shoulder]</char> in mount Efrayim <char style="add">[Doubly Fruitful]</char>, and dwelt in it; and went out from there, and built P’nu’el <char style="add">[Facing God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> said in his heart, Now shall the kingdom return to the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />If this people go up to do sacrifice in the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> at Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, then shall the heart of this people turn again unto their lord, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and they shall kill me, and go again to Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Whereupon the king took counsel, and made two calves <char style="add">[of]</char> gold, and said unto them, It is too much for you to go up to Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>: behold your<char style="ord">i</char> gods, O Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which brought you<char style="ord">i</char> up out of the land of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And he set the one in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and the other put he in Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And this thing became a sin: for the people went <char style="add">[to worship]</char> before the one, <char style="add">[even]</char> unto Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And he made an house of high places, and made priests of the lowest of the people, which were not of the sons of Levi <char style="pn">(Levite)</char> <char style="add">[Adhesion, Joiner]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> ordained a feast in the eighth month, on the fifteenth day of the month, like unto the feast that <char style="add">[is]</char> in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and he offered upon the altar. So did he in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, sacrificing unto the calves that he had made: and he placed in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> the priests of the high places which he had made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />So he offered upon the altar which he had made in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char> the fifteenth day of the eighth month, <char style="add">[even]</char> in the month which he had devised of his own heart; and ordained a feast unto the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and he offered upon the altar, and burnt incense.</para>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And, behold, there came a man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> out of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> by the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> unto Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>: and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> stood by the altar to burn incense.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he cried against the altar in the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, O altar, altar, thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; Behold, a child shall be born unto the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, Yoshiyahu <char style="add">[whom Yehovah heals]</char> by name; and upon you<char style="ord">i</char> shall he offer the priests of the high places that burn incense upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and men’s bones shall be burnt upon you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he gave a sign the same day, saying, This <char style="add">[is]</char> the sign which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken; Behold, the altar shall be rent, and the ashes that <char style="add">[are]</char> upon it shall be poured out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it came to pass, when king Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> heard the saying of the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, which had cried against the altar in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, that he put forth his hand from the altar, saying, Lay hold on him. And his hand, which he put forth against him, dried up, so that he could not pull it in again to him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />The altar also was rent, and the ashes poured out from the altar, according to the sign which the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had given by the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the king answered and said unto the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, Entreat now the face of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and pray for me, that my hand may be restored me again. And the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> besought the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the king’s hand was restored him again, and became as <char style="add">[it was]</char> before.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the king said unto the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, Come home with me, and refresh yourself, and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> a reward.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> said unto the king, If you<char style="ord">i</char> will give me half your<char style="ord">i</char> house, I will not go in with you<char style="ord">i</char>, neither will I eat bread nor drink water in this place:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For so was it charged me by the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Eat no bread, nor drink water, nor turn again by the same way that you<char style="ord">i</char> came.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So he went another way, and returned not by the way that he came to Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Now there dwelt an old prophet in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>; and his sons came and told him all the works that the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> had done that day in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>: the words which he had spoken unto the king, them they told also to their father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And their father said unto them, What way went he? For his sons had seen what way the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> went, which came from Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And he said unto his sons, Saddle me the ass. So they saddled him the ass: and he rode thereon,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And went after the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and found him sitting under an oak: and he said unto him, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> that came from Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>? And he said, I <char style="add">[am]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then he said unto him, Come home with me, and eat bread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he said, I may not return with you<char style="ord">i</char>, nor go in with you<char style="ord">i</char>: neither will I eat bread nor drink water with you<char style="ord">i</char> in this place:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />For it was said to me by the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall eat no bread nor drink water there, nor turn again to go by the way that you<char style="ord">i</char> came.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />He said unto him, I <char style="add">[am]</char> a prophet also as you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char>; and an angel spoke unto me by the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, Bring him back with you<char style="ord">i</char> into your<char style="ord">i</char> house, that he may eat bread and drink water. <char style="add">[But]</char> he lied unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />So he went back with him, and did eat bread in his house, and drank water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And it came to pass, as they sat at the table, that the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto the prophet that brought him back:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he cried unto the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> that came from Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Forasmuch as you<char style="ord">i</char> have disobeyed the mouth of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and have not kept the commandment which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> commanded you<char style="ord">i</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But came back, and have eaten bread and drunk water in the place, of the which [the LORD-Yehōvah (Messiah Pre-Incarnate)] did say to you<char style="ord">i</char>, Eat no bread, and drink no water; your<char style="ord">i</char> carcass shall not come unto the sepulcher of your<char style="ord">i</char> fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And it came to pass, after he had eaten bread, and after he had drunk, that he saddled for him the ass, <char style="add">[that is to say]</char>, for the prophet whom he had brought back.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And when he was gone, a lion met him by the way, and killed him: and his carcass was cast in the way, and the ass stood by it, the lion also stood by the carcass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And, behold, men passed by, and saw the carcass cast in the way, and the lion standing by the carcass: and they came and told <char style="add">[it]</char> in the city where the old prophet dwelt.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And when the prophet that brought him back from the way heard <char style="add">[thereof]</char>, he said, It <char style="add">[is]</char> the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, who was disobedient unto the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: therefore the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has delivered him unto the lion, which has torn him, and slain him, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke unto him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And he spoke to his sons, saying, Saddle me the ass. And they saddled <char style="add">[him]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And he went and found his carcass cast in the way, and the ass and the lion standing by the carcass: the lion had not eaten the carcass, nor torn the ass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And the prophet took up the carcass of the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and laid it upon the ass, and brought it back: and the old prophet came to the city, to mourn and to bury him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And he laid his carcass in his own grave; and they mourned over him, <char style="add">[saying]</char>, Alas, my brother!</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And it came to pass, after he had buried him, that he spoke to his sons, saying, When I am dead, then bury me in the sepulcher wherein the man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered] [is]</char> buried; lay my bones beside his bones:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />For the saying which he cried by the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> against the altar in Beit-El <char style="add">[House of God]</char>, and against all the houses of the high places which <char style="add">[are]</char> in the cities of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, shall surely come to pass.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />After this thing Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> returned not from his evil way, but made again of the lowest of the people priests of the high places: whosoever would, he consecrated him, and he became <char style="add">[one]</char> of the priests of the high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And this thing became sin unto the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, even to cut <char style="add">[it]</char> off, and to destroy <char style="add">[it]</char> from off the face of the earth.</para>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />At that time Aviyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is (my) father]</char> the son of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> fell sick.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> said to his wife, Arise, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, and disguise yourself, that you<char style="ord">i</char> be not known to be the wife of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>; and get you<char style="ord">i</char> to Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>: behold, there <char style="add">[is]</char> Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> the prophet, which told me that <char style="add">[I should be]</char> king over this people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And take with you<char style="ord">i</char> ten loaves, and cracknels <char style="pn">(dry, brittle cakes or buscuits)</char>, and a pot of honey, and go to him: he shall tell you<char style="ord">i</char> what shall become of the child.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Yarov’am’s <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> wife did so, and arose, and went to Shiloh <char style="add">[Place of Rest]</char>, and came to the house of Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>. But Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> could not see; for his eyes were set by reason of his age.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>, Behold, the wife of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> comes to ask a thing of you<char style="ord">i</char> for her son; for he <char style="add">[is]</char> sick: thus and thus shall you<char style="ord">i</char> say unto her: for it shall be, when she comes in, that she shall feign <char style="pn">(to pretend to be; to disguise)</char> herself <char style="add">[to be]</char> another <char style="add">[woman]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, when Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> heard the sound of her feet, as she came in at the door, that he said, Come in, you<char style="ord">i</char> wife of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>; why pretend you<char style="ord">i</char> yourself <char style="add">[to be]</char> another? for I <char style="add">[am]</char> sent to you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[with]</char> heavy <char style="add">[tidings]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Go, tell Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Forasmuch as I exalted you<char style="ord">i</char> from among the people, and made you<char style="ord">i</char> prince over my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And rent the kingdom away from the house of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, and gave it you<char style="ord">i</char>: and <char style="add">[yet]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have not been as my servant David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>, who kept my commandments, and who followed me with all his heart, to do <char style="add">[that]</char> only <char style="add">[which was]</char> right in my eyes;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />But have done evil above all that were before you<char style="ord">i</char>: for you<char style="ord">i</char> have gone and made you<char style="ord">i</char> other gods, and molten images, to provoke me to anger, and have cast me behind your<char style="ord">i</char> back:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />Therefore, behold, I will bring evil upon the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, and will cut off from Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> him that pisses against the wall, <char style="add">[and]</char> him that is shut up and left in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and will take away the remnant of the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, as a man takes away dung, till it be all gone.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />Him that dies of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> in the city shall the dogs eat; and him that dies in the field shall the fowls of the air eat: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Arise you<char style="ord">i</char> therefore, get you<char style="ord">i</char> to your<char style="ord">i</char> own house: <char style="add">[and]</char> when your<char style="ord">i</char> feet enter into the city, the child shall die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall mourn for him, and bury him: for he only of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> shall come to the grave, because in him there is found <char style="add">[some]</char> good thing toward the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Moreover the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall raise him up a king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, who shall cut off the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> that day: but what <char style="pn">(will God do)</char> even now?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />For the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall strike Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, as a reed is shaken in the water, and he shall root up Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> out of this good land, which he gave to their fathers, and shall scatter them beyond the river, because they have made their groves, provoking the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> to anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And he shall give Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> up because of the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, who did sin, and who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Yarov’am’s <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> wife arose, and departed, and came to Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>: <char style="add">[and]</char> when she came to the threshold of the door, the child died;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And they buried him; and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> mourned for him, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke by the hand of his servant Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> the prophet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And the rest of the acts of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, how he warred, and how he reigned, behold, they <char style="add">[are]</char> written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the days which Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> reigned <char style="add">[were]</char> two and twenty years: and he slept with his fathers, and Nadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> the son of Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> reigned in Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>. Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged] [was]</char> forty and one years old when he began to reign, and he reigned seventeen years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, the city which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> did choose out of all the tribes of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, to put his name there. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Na’amah <char style="add">[Loveliness]</char> an ‘Amonit <char style="add">[tribal]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and they provoked him to jealousy with their sins which they had committed, above all that their fathers had done.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />For they also built them high places, and images, and groves, on every high hill, and under every green tree.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And there were also sodomites in the land: <char style="add">[and]</char> they did according to all the abominations of the nations which the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> cast out before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And it came to pass in the fifth year of king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char>, <char style="add">[that]</char> Shishak <char style="add">[greedy of fine linen]</char> king of Mitzrayim <char style="add">[Egypt - The Narrow Place]</char> came up against Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he took away the treasures of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the treasures of the king’s house; he even took away all: and he took away all the shields of gold which Shlomo <char style="pn">(Solomon)</char> <char style="add">[peace]</char> had made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And king Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> made in their stead brazen shields, and committed <char style="add">[them]</char> unto the hands of the chief of the guard, which kept the door of the king’s house.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, when the king went into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that the guard bore them, and brought them back into the guard chamber.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And there was war between Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> all <char style="add">[their]</char> days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Na’amah <char style="add">[Loveliness]</char> an ‘Amonit <char style="add">[tribal]</char>. And Aviyam <char style="add">[Yah is my father]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Now in the eighteenth year of king Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char> reigned Aviyam <char style="add">[Yah is my father]</char> over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Three years reigned he in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression]</char>, the daughter of Avishalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And he walked in all the sins of his father, which he had done before him: and his heart was not perfect with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, as the heart of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Nevertheless for David’s <char style="add">[beloved]</char>’s sake did the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> his God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> give him a lamp in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>, to set up his son after him, and to establish Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Because David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and turned not aside from any <char style="add">[thing]</char> that he commanded him all the days of his life, save only in the matter of Uriyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is my light (flame)]</char> the Hitti <char style="add">[Terrorists]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And there was war between Rechav’am <char style="add">[a people has enlarged]</char> and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> all the days of his life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Aviyam <char style="add">[Yah is my father]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>? And there was war between Aviyam <char style="add">[Yah is my father]</char> and Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And Aviyam <char style="add">[Yah is my father]</char> slept with his fathers; and they buried him in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char>: and Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And in the twentieth year of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> reigned Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And forty and one years reigned he in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression]</char>, the daughter of Avishalom <char style="add">[my father is peace]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> did <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, as <char style="add">[did]</char> David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And he took away the sodomites out of the land, and removed all the idols that his fathers had made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And also Ma’akhah <char style="add">[oppression]</char> his mother, even her he removed from <char style="add">[being]</char> queen, because she had made an idol in a grove; and Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> destroyed her idol, and burnt <char style="add">[it]</char> by the brook Kidron <char style="add">[dark]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />But the high places were not removed: nevertheless Asa’s <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> heart was perfect with the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> all his days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And he brought in the things which his father had dedicated, and the things which himself had dedicated, into the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, silver, and gold, and vessels.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And there was war between Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> and Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> all their days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went up against Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and built Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, that he might not suffer any to go out or come in to Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Then Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> took all the silver and the gold <char style="add">[that were]</char> left in the treasures of the house of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and the treasures of the king’s house, and delivered them into the hand of his servants: and king Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> sent them to Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char>, the son of Tavirmmon <char style="add">[good is pomegranate]</char>, the son of Hezyon <char style="add">[vision]</char>, king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, that dwelt at Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There is]</char> a league between me and you<char style="ord">i</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> between my father and your<char style="ord">i</char> father: behold, I have sent unto you<char style="ord">i</char> a present of silver and gold; come and break your<char style="ord">i</char> league with Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that he may depart from me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />So Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> listened unto king Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>, and sent the captains of the hosts which he had against the cities of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and struck ‘Iyon <char style="add">[a ruin]</char>, and Dan <char style="add">[Judge]</char>, and Avel-Beit-Ma’akhah <char style="add">[meadow of the house of oppression]</char>, and all Kinn’rot <char style="add">[harps]</char>, with all the land of Naftali <char style="add">[My Wrestling]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> heard <char style="add">[thereof]</char>, that he left off building of Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, and dwelt in Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then king Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> made a proclamation throughout all Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>; none <char style="add">[was]</char> exempted: and they took away the stones of Ramah <char style="add">[Hill]</char>, and the timber thereof, which Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> had built; and king Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> built with them Geva <char style="add">[hill]</char> of Binyamin <char style="add">[Son of the Right Hand/Strength]</char>, and Mitzpah <char style="add">[watchtower]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />The rest of all the acts of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>, and all his might, and all that he did, and the cities which he built, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>? Nevertheless in the time of his old age he was diseased in his feet.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father: and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Nadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char> the son of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> began to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in the second year of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and reigned over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> two years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and walked in the way of his father, and in his sin which he made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> the son of Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>, of the house of Yissakhar <char style="add">[There Is Recompense]</char>, conspired against him; and Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> struck him at Gib’ton <char style="add">[mound]</char>, which <char style="add">[belonged]</char> to the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>; for Nadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char> and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> laid siege to Gib’ton <char style="add">[mound]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />Even in the third year of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> did Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> slay him, and reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And it came to pass, when he reigned, <char style="add">[that]</char> he struck all the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>; he left not to Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> any that breathed, until he had destroyed him, according unto the saying of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke by his servant Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> the Shiloni <char style="add">[peace bringer] [place of rest]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />Because of the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> which he sinned, and which he made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> sin, by his provocation which he provoked the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to anger.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Nadav <char style="add">[Generous]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And there was war between Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> and Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> all their days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />In the third year of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> the son of Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char> to reign over all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>, twenty and four years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And he did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and walked in the way of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, and in his sin which he made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />Then the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Hanani <char style="add">[gracious]</char> against Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Forasmuch as I exalted you<char style="ord">i</char> out of the dust, and made you<char style="ord">i</char> prince over my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; and you<char style="ord">i</char> have walked in the way of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, and have made my people Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin, to provoke me to anger with their sins;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Behold, I will take away the posterity of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char>, and the posterity of his house; and will make you<char style="ord">i</char> house like the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />Him that dies of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> in the city shall the dogs eat; and him that dies of his in the fields shall the fowls of the air eat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char>, and what he did, and his might, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried in Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>: and Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And also by the hand of the prophet Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Hanani <char style="add">[gracious]</char> came the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> against Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char>, and against his house, even for all the evil that he did in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, in provoking him to anger with the work of his hands, in being like the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>; and because he killed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />In the twenty and sixth year of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char> the son of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>, two years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And his servant Zimri <char style="add">[My Music]</char>, captain of half <char style="add">[his]</char> chariots, conspired against him, as he was in Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>, drinking himself drunk in the house of Artza <char style="add">[earthy]</char> steward of <char style="add">[his]</char> house in Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Zimri <char style="add">[My Music]</char> went in and struck him, and killed him, in the twenty and seventh year of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And it came to pass, when he began to reign, as soon as he sat on his throne, <char style="add">[that]</char> he killed all the house of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char>: he left him not one that pisses against a wall, neither of his relatives, nor of his friends.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />Thus did Zimri <char style="add">[My Music]</char> destroy all the house of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char>, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke against Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> by Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the prophet,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />For all the sins of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char>, and the sins of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char> his son, by which they sinned, and by which they made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin, in provoking the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to anger with their vanities.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Elah <char style="add">[an oak]</char>, and all that he did, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />In the twenty and seventh year of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> did Zimri <char style="add">[My Music]</char> reign seven days in Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>. And the people <char style="add">[were]</char> encamped against Gib’ton <char style="add">[mound]</char>, which <char style="add">[belonged]</char> to the P’lishtim <char style="add">[Immigrants]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the people <char style="add">[that were]</char> encamped heard say, Zimri <char style="add">[My Music]</char> has conspired, and has also slain the king: wherefore all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> made ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char>, the captain of the host, king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that day in the camp.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> went up from Gib’ton <char style="add">[mound]</char>, and all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> with him, and they besieged Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Zimri <char style="add">[My Music]</char> saw that the city was taken, that he went into the palace of the king’s house, and burnt the king’s house over him with fire, and died,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />For his sins which he sinned in doing evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, in walking in the way of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char>, and in his sin which he did, to make Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Zimri <char style="add">[My Music]</char>, and his treason that he wrought, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Then were the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> divided into two parts: half of the people followed Tivni <char style="add">[intelligent]</char> the son of Ginat <char style="add">[protection]</char>, to make him king; and half followed ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />But the people that followed ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> prevailed against the people that followed Tivni <char style="add">[intelligent]</char> the son of Ginat <char style="add">[protection]</char>: so Tivni <char style="add">[intelligent]</char> died, and ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> reigned.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />In the thirty and first year of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, twelve years: six years reigned he in Tirtzah <char style="add">[Favourable]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And he bought the hill Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> of Shemer <char style="add">[preserved]</char> for two talents of silver, and built on the hill, and called the name of the city which he built, after the name of Shemer <char style="add">[preserved]</char>, owner of the hill, Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> wrought evil in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and did worse than all that <char style="add">[were]</char> before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />For he walked in all the way of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, and in his sin which he made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin, to provoke the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to anger with their vanities.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> which he did, and his might that he showed, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />So ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>: and Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And in the thirty and eighth year of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> began Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> the son of ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> the son of ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> reigned over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> twenty and two years.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> the son of ‘Omri <char style="add">[pupil of Yehovah]</char> did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> above all that <char style="add">[were]</char> before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And it came to pass, as if it had been a light thing for him to walk in the sins of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, that he took to wife Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> the daughter of Etba’al <char style="add">[with Ba’al]</char> king of the people of Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and went and served Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and worshipped him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And he reared up an altar for Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> in the house of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, which he had built in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> made a grove; and Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> did more to provoke the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to anger than all the kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> that were before him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />In his days did Hi’el <char style="add">[God lives]</char> the Beit-Eli <char style="add">[House of God]</char> build Yericho <char style="add">[Its Moon]</char>: he laid the foundation thereof in Aviram <char style="add">[My Father is Exalted]</char> his firstborn, and set up the gates thereof in his youngest <char style="add">[son]</char> S’guv <char style="add">[exalted]</char>, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke by Y’hoshua <char style="add">[Yehovah is Salvation]</char> the son of Nun <char style="add">[Posterity]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the Tishbi <char style="add">[captivity]</char>, <char style="add">[who was]</char> of the inhabitants of Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region]</char>, said unto Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> lives, before whom I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to my word.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto him, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Get you<char style="ord">i</char> hence, and turn you<char style="ord">i</char> eastward, and hide yourself by the brook K’rit <char style="add">[cutting]</char>, that <char style="add">[is]</char> before Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> shall drink of the brook; and I have commanded the ravens to feed you<char style="ord">i</char> there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />So he went and did according unto the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: for he went and dwelt by the brook K’rit <char style="add">[cutting]</char>, that <char style="add">[is]</char> before Yarden <char style="add">[Descender]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And the ravens brought him bread and flesh in the morning, and bread and flesh in the evening; and he drank of the brook.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And it came to pass after a while, that the brook dried up, because there had been no rain in the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came unto him, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Arise, get you<char style="ord">i</char> to Tzarfat <char style="add">[refinery]</char>, which <char style="add">[belongs]</char> to Tzidon <char style="add">[Hunting]</char>, and dwell there: behold, I have commanded a widow woman there to sustain you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />So he arose and went to Tzarfat <char style="add">[refinery]</char>. And when he came to the gate of the city, behold, the widow woman <char style="add">[was]</char> there gathering of sticks: and he called to her, and said, Fetch me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, a little water in a vessel, that I may drink.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And as she was going to fetch <char style="add">[it]</char>, he called to her, and said, Bring me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, a morsel of bread in your<char style="ord">i</char> hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And she said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> lives, I have not a cake, but an handful of meal in a barrel, and a little oil in a pot: and, behold, I <char style="add">[am]</char> gathering two sticks, that I may go in and dress it for me and my son, that we may eat it, and die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto her, Fear not; go <char style="add">[and]</char> do as you<char style="ord">i</char> have said: but make me thereof a little cake first, and bring <char style="add">[it]</char> unto me, and after make for you<char style="ord">i</char> and for your<char style="ord">i</char> son.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />For thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, The barrel of meal shall not waste, neither shall the pot of oil fail, until the day <char style="add">[that]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> send rain upon the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And she went and did according to the saying of Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>: and she, and he, and her house, did eat <char style="add">[many]</char> days.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[And]</char> the barrel of meal wasted not, neither did the pot of oil fail, according to the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, which he spoke by Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it came to pass after these things, <char style="add">[that]</char> the son of the woman, the mistress of the house, fell sick; and his sickness was so sore, that there was no breath left in him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And she said unto Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, What have I to do with you<char style="ord">i</char>, O you<char style="ord">i</char> man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>? are you<char style="ord">i</char> come unto me to call my sin to remembrance, and to slay my son?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he said unto her, Give me your<char style="ord">i</char> son. And he took him out of her bosom, and carried him up into a loft, where he abode, and laid him upon his own bed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, have you<char style="ord">i</char> also brought evil upon the widow with whom I sojourn, by slaying her son?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he stretched himself upon the child three times, and cried unto the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> my God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let this child’s soul come into him again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> heard the voice of Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>; and the soul of the child came into him again, and he revived.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> took the child, and brought him down out of the chamber into the house, and delivered him unto his mother: and Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said, See, your<char style="ord">i</char> son lives.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And the woman said to Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, Now by this I know that you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> a man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, <char style="add">[and]</char> that the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> in your<char style="ord">i</char> mouth <char style="add">[is]</char> truth.</para>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass <char style="add">[after]</char> many days, that the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> in the third year, saying, Go, show yourself unto Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>; and I will send rain upon the earth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> went to show himself unto Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>. And <char style="add">[there was]</char> a sore famine in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> called ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char>, which <char style="add">[was]</char> the governor of <char style="add">[his]</char> house. (Now ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char> feared the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> greatly:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />For it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, when Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> cut off the prophets of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, that ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char> took an hundred prophets, and hid them by fifty in a cave, and fed them with bread and water.)</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> said unto ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char>, Go into the land, unto all fountains of water, and unto all brooks: perhaps we may find grass to save the horses and mules alive, that we lose not all the beasts.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />So they divided the land between them to pass throughout it: Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> went one way by himself, and ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char> went another way by himself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And as ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char> was in the way, behold, Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> met him: and he knew him, and fell on his face, and said, <char style="add">[Is it really]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> my lord Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he answered him, I <char style="add">[am]</char>: go, tell your<char style="ord">i</char> lord, Behold, Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah] [is here]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he said, What have I sinned, that you<char style="ord">i</char> would deliver your<char style="ord">i</char> servant into the hand of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, to slay me?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> lives, there is no nation or kingdom, to which my lord has not sent to seek you<char style="ord">i</char>: and when they said, <char style="add">[He is]</char> not <char style="add">[there]</char>; he took an oath of the kingdom and nation, that they found you<char style="ord">i</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And now you<char style="ord">i</char> say, Go, tell your<char style="ord">i</char> lord, Behold, Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah] [is here]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[as soon as]</char> I am gone from you<char style="ord">i</char>, that the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall carry you<char style="ord">i</char> to where I know not; and <char style="add">[so]</char> when I come and tell Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, and he cannot find you<char style="ord">i</char>, he shall slay me: but I your<char style="ord">i</char> servant fear the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> from my youth.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />Was it not told my lord what I did when Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> killed the prophets of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, how I hid an hundred men of the LORD-Yehōvah’s <char style="add">[Messiah Pre-Incarnate]</char> prophets by fifty in a cave, and fed them with bread and water?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And now you<char style="ord">i</char> say, Go, tell your<char style="ord">i</char> lord, Behold, Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah] [is here]</char>: and he shall slay me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char> lives, before whom I stand, I will surely show myself unto him to day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />So ‘Ovadyah <char style="add">[servant of Yehovah]</char> went to meet Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, and told him: and Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> went to meet Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> saw Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, that Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> said unto him, <char style="add">[Are]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> he that troubles Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he answered, I have not troubled Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>; but you<char style="ord">i</char>, and your<char style="ord">i</char> father’s house, in that you<char style="ord">2f</char> have forsaken the commandments of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and you<char style="ord">i</char> have followed Ba’alim <char style="add">[lords (false gods)]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />Now therefore send, <char style="add">[and]</char> gather to me all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> unto mount Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>, and the prophets of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> four hundred and fifty, and the prophets of the groves four hundred, which eat at Izevel’s <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> table.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />So Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> sent unto all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and gathered the prophets together unto mount Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> came unto all the people, and said, How long lame <char style="pn">(crippled in the feet)</char> you<char style="ord">2f</char> between two opinions? if the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[be]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, follow him: but if Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, <char style="add">[then]</char> follow him. And the people answered him not a word.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />Then said Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> unto the people, I, <char style="add">[even]</char> I only, remain a prophet of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; but Ba’al’s [lord (a false god)] prophets <char style="add">[are]</char> four hundred and fifty men.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Let them therefore give us two bullocks; and let them choose one bullock for themselves, and cut it in pieces, and lay <char style="add">[it]</char> on wood, and put no fire <char style="add">[under]</char>: and I will dress the other bullock, and lay <char style="add">[it]</char> on wood, and put no fire <char style="add">[under]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And call you<char style="ord">2f</char> on the name of your gods, and I will call on the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> that answers by fire, let him be God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>. And all the people answered and said, It is well spoken.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto the prophets of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, Choose you one bullock for yourselves, and dress <char style="add">[it]</char> first; for you<char style="ord">2f</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> many; and call on the name of your gods, but put no fire <char style="add">[under]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And they took the bullock which was given them, and they dressed <char style="add">[it]</char>, and called on the name of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char> from morning even until noon, saying, O Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, hear us. But <char style="add">[there was]</char> no voice, nor any that answered. And they leaped upon the altar which was made.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And it came to pass at noon, that Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> mocked them, and said, Cry aloud: for he <char style="add">[is]</char> a god; either he is talking, or he is pursuing, or he is in a journey, <char style="add">[or]</char> perhaps he sleeps, and must be awakened.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And they cried aloud, and cut themselves after their manner with knives and lancets, till the blood gushed out upon them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And it came to pass, when midday was past, and they prophesied until the <char style="add">[time]</char> of the offering of the <char style="add">[evening]</char> sacrifice, that <char style="add">[there was]</char> neither voice, nor any to answer, nor any that regarded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto all the people, Come near unto me. And all the people came near unto him. And he repaired the altar of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[that was]</char> broken down.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> took twelve stones, according to the number of the tribes of the sons of Ya’akov <char style="add">[Heal of God]</char>, unto whom the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came, saying, Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> shall be your<char style="ord">i</char> name:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And with the stones he built an altar in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: and he made a trench about the altar, as great as would contain two measures of seed.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And he put the wood in order, and cut the bullock in pieces, and laid <char style="add">[him]</char> on the wood, and said, Fill four barrels with water, and pour <char style="add">[it]</char> on the burnt sacrifice, and on the wood.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And he said, Do <char style="add">[it]</char> the second time. And they did <char style="add">[it]</char> the second time. And he said, Do <char style="add">[it]</char> the third time. And they did <char style="add">[it]</char> the third time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the water ran round about the altar; and he filled the trench also with water.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And it came to pass at <char style="add">[the time of]</char> the offering of the <char style="add">[evening]</char> sacrifice, that Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the prophet came near, and said, LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Avraham <char style="add">[Exalted Father]</char>, Yitz’khak <char style="add">[Laughter]</char>, and of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, let it be known this day that you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and <char style="add">[that]</char> I <char style="add">[am]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> servant, and <char style="add">[that]</char> I have done all these things at your<char style="ord">i</char> word.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Hear me, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, hear me, that this people may know that you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and <char style="add">[that]</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> have turned their heart back again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />Then the fire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> fell, and consumed the burnt sacrifice, and the wood, and the stones, and the dust, and licked up the water that <char style="add">[was]</char> in the trench.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And when all the people saw <char style="add">[it]</char>, they fell on their faces: and they said, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, he <char style="add">[is]</char> the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>; the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, he <char style="add">[is]</char> the God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto them, Take the prophets of Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>; let not one of them escape. And they took them: and Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> brought them down to the brook Kishon <char style="add">[Winding]</char>, and killed them there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> said unto Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, Get you<char style="ord">i</char> up, eat and drink; for <char style="add">[there is]</char> a sound of abundance of rain.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />So Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>went up to eat and to drink. And Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> went up to the top of Carmel <char style="add">[Garden-land]</char>; and he cast himself down upon the earth, and put his face between his knees,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And said to his servant, Go up now, look toward the sea. And he went up, and looked, and said, <char style="add">[There is]</char> nothing. And he said, Go again seven times.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And it came to pass at the seventh time, that he said, Behold, there arises a little cloud out of the sea, like a man’s hand. And he said, Go up, say unto Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, Prepare <char style="add">[you<char style="ord">i</char> chariot]</char>, and get you<char style="ord">i</char> down, that the rain stop you<char style="ord">i</char> not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />And it came to pass in the meanwhile, that the heaven was black with clouds and wind, and there was a great rain. And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> rode, and went to Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />And the hand of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> was on Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>; and he girded up his waist, and ran before Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> to the entrance of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> told Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> all that Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> had done, and withal how he had slain all the prophets with the sword.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />Then Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> sent a messenger unto Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, saying, So let the gods do <char style="add">[to me]</char>, and more also, if I make not your<char style="ord">i</char> life as the life of one of them by tomorrow about this time.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And when he saw <char style="add">[that]</char>, he arose, and went for his life, and came to Be’er-sheva <char style="add">[Well of the sevenfold Oath]</char>, which <char style="add">[belongs]</char> to Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and left his servant there.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />But he himself went a day’s journey into the wilderness, and came and sat down under a juniper tree: and he requested for himself that he might die; and said, It is enough; now, O LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, take away my life; for I <char style="add">[am]</char> not better than my fathers.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And as he lay and slept under a juniper tree, behold, then an angel <char style="add">[Mal’ach]</char> touched him, and said unto him, Arise <char style="add">[and]</char> eat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he looked, and, behold, <char style="add">[there was]</char> a cake baked on the coals, and a pot of water at his head. And he did eat and drink, and laid him down again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And the angel of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came again the second time, and touched him, and said, Arise <char style="add">[and]</char> eat; because the journey <char style="add">[is]</char> too great for you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And he arose, and did eat and drink, and went in the strength of that meat forty days and forty nights unto Horev <char style="add">[Desert]</char> the mount of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And he came there unto a cave, and lodged there; and, behold, the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[came]</char> to him, and he said unto him, What do you<char style="ord">i</char> here, Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And he said, I have been very jealous for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>: for the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> have forsaken you<char style="ord">i</char> covenant, thrown down you<char style="ord">i</char> altars, and slain you<char style="ord">i</char> prophets with the sword; and I, <char style="add">[even]</char> I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And he said, Go forth, and stand upon the mount before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>. And, behold, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> passed by, and a great and strong wind rent the mountains, and broke in pieces the rocks before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>; <char style="add">[but]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> not in the wind: and after the wind an earthquake; <char style="add">[but]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> not in the earthquake:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And after the earthquake a fire; <char style="add">[but]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[was]</char> not in the fire: and after the fire a still small voice.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And it was <char style="add">[so]</char>, when Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> heard <char style="add">[it]</char>, that he wrapped his face in his Mantle <char style="pn">(cloak; covering garment)</char> <char style="pn">(cloak)</char>, and went out, and stood in the entering in of the cave. And, behold, <char style="add">[there came]</char> a voice unto him, and said, What do you<char style="ord">i</char> here, Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And he said, I have been very jealous for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> Tz’va’ot <char style="add">[of the Heavenly Armies]</char>: because the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> have forsaken your<char style="ord">i</char> covenant, thrown down your<char style="ord">i</char> altars, and slain your<char style="ord">i</char> prophets with the sword; and I, <char style="add">[even]</char> I only, am left; and they seek my life, to take it away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, Go, return on you<char style="ord">i</char> way to the wilderness of Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>: and when you<char style="ord">i</char> come, anoint Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God] [to be]</char> king over Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> the son of Nimshi <char style="add">[rescued]</char> shall you<char style="ord">i</char> anoint <char style="add">[to be]</char> king over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: and Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> the son of Shafat <char style="add">[He Has Judged]</char> of Avel-M’cholah <char style="add">[Meadow of Dancing]</char> shall you<char style="ord">i</char> anoint <char style="add">[to be]</char> prophet in your<char style="ord">i</char> room.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And it shall come to pass, <char style="add">[that]</char> him that escapes the sword of Haza’el <char style="add">[one who sees God]</char> shall Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> slay: and him that escapes from the sword of Yehu <char style="add">[Yehovah is He]</char> shall Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> slay.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Yet I have left <char style="add">[me]</char> seven thousand in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, all the knees which have not bowed unto Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and every mouth which has not kissed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />So he departed there, and found Eli-sha <char style="add">[my God is salvation]</char> the son of Shafat <char style="add">[He Has Judged]</char>, who <char style="add">[was]</char> plowing <char style="add">[with]</char> twelve yoke <char style="add">[of oxen]</char> before him, and he with the twelfth: and Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> passed by him, and cast his Mantle <char style="pn">(cloak; covering garment)</char> <char style="pn">(cloak)</char> upon him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And he left the oxen, and ran after Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, and said, Let me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, kiss my father and my mother, and <char style="add">[then]</char> I will follow you<char style="ord">i</char>. And he said unto him, Go <char style="pn">(and return)</char> back again: for what I have done to you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And he returned back from him, and took a yoke of oxen, and killed them, and boiled their flesh with the instruments of the oxen, and gave unto the people, and they did eat. Then he arose, and went after Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, and ministered unto him.</para>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And Ben-Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> gathered all his host together: and <char style="add">[there were]</char> thirty and two kings with him, and horses, and chariots: and he went up and besieged Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>, and warred against it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And he sent messengers to Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> into the city, and said unto him, Thus says Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />Your<char style="ord">1s</char> silver and your<char style="ord">i</char> gold <char style="add">[is]</char> my; your<char style="ord">i</char> wives also and your<char style="ord">i</char> children, <char style="add">[even]</char> the best, <char style="add">[are]</char> my.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> answered and said, My lord, O king, according to your<char style="ord">i</char> saying, I <char style="add">[am]</char> yoursi, and all that I have.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And the messengers came again, and said, Thus speaks Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char>, saying, Although I have sent unto you<char style="ord">i</char>, saying, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall deliver me your<char style="ord">i</char> silver, and your<char style="ord">i</char> gold, and your<char style="ord">i</char> wives, and your<char style="ord">i</char> children;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Yet I will send my servants unto you<char style="ord">i</char> tomorrow about this time, and they shall search your<char style="ord">i</char> house, and the houses of your<char style="ord">i</char> servants; and it shall be, <char style="add">[that]</char> whatsoever is pleasant in your<char style="ord">i</char> eyes, they shall put <char style="add">[it]</char> in their hand, and take <char style="add">[it]</char> away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />Then the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> called all the elders of the land, and said, Mark, I pray you, and see how this <char style="add">[man]</char> seeks mischief: for he sent unto me for my wives, and for my children, and for my silver, and for my gold; and I denied him not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And all the elders and all the people said unto him, Listen not <char style="add">[unto him]</char>, nor consent.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />For what reason he said unto the messengers of Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char>, Tell my lord the king, All that you<char style="ord">i</char> did send for to your<char style="ord">i</char> servant at the first I will do: but this thing I may not do. And the messengers departed, and brought him word again.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> sent unto him, and said, The gods do so unto me, and more also, if the dust of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> shall suffice for handfuls for all the people that follow me.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> answered and said, Tell <char style="add">[him]</char>, Let not him that put on <char style="add">[his harness]</char> boast himself as he that puts it off.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And it came to pass, when <char style="add">[Ben-Hadad [son of the (false god) Hadad]]</char> heard this message, as he <char style="add">[was]</char> drinking, he and the kings in the pavilions, that he said unto his servants, Set <char style="add">[yourselves in array (to put on; to clothe)]</char>. And they set <char style="add">[themselves in array (to put on; to clothe)]</char> against the city.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And, behold, there came a prophet unto Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Have you<char style="ord">i</char> seen all this great multitude? behold, I will deliver it into your<char style="ord">i</char> hand this day; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> said, By whom? And he said, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, <char style="add">[Even]</char> by the young men of the princes of the provinces. Then he said, Who shall order the battle? And he answered, you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />Then he numbered the young men of the princes of the provinces, and they were two hundred and thirty two: and after them he numbered all the people, <char style="add">[even]</char> all the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, <char style="add">[being]</char> seven thousand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And they went out at noon. But Ben-Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] <char style="add">[was]</char> drinking himself drunk in the pavilions, he and the kings, the thirty and two kings that helped him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the young men of the princes of the provinces went out first; and Ben-Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] sent out, and they told him, saying, There are men come out of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And he said, Whether they be come out for peace, take them alive; or whether they be come out for war, take them alive.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />So these young men of the princes of the provinces came out of the city, and the army which followed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And they killed everyone his man: and the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> fled; and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> pursued them: and Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> escaped on an horse with the horsemen.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went out, and struck the horses and chariots, and killed the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> with a great slaughter.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the prophet came to the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and said unto him, Go, strengthen yourself, and mark, and see what you<char style="ord">i</char> do: for at the return of the year the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> will come up against you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And the servants of the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> said unto him, Their gods <char style="add">[are]</char> gods of the hills; therefore they were stronger than we; but let us fight against them in the plain, and surely we shall be stronger than they.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />And do this thing, Take the kings away, every man out of his place, and put captains in their rooms:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And number you<char style="ord">i</char> an army, like the army that you<char style="ord">i</char> have lost, horse for horse, and chariot for chariot: and we will fight against them in the plain, <char style="add">[and]</char> surely we shall be stronger than they. And he listened unto their voice, and did so.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And it came to pass at the return of the year, that Ben-Hadad [son of the <char style="pn">(false god)</char> Hadad] numbered the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>, and went up to Aphek <char style="add">[Enclosure]</char>, to fight against Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> were numbered, and were all present, and went against them: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> pitched before them like two little herds of goats; but the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> filled the country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And there came a man of God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char>, and spoke unto the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and said, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Because the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> have said, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> <char style="add">[is]</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the hills, but he <char style="add">[is]</char> not God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of the valleys, therefore will I deliver all this great multitude into your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and you<char style="ord">2f</char> shall know that I <char style="add">[am]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />And they pitched one over against the other seven days. And <char style="add">[so]</char> it was, that in the seventh day the battle was joined: and the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> killed of the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char> an hundred thousand footmen in one day.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />But the rest fled to Aphek <char style="add">[Enclosure]</char>, into the city; and <char style="add">[there]</char> a wall fell upon twenty and seven thousand of the men <char style="add">[that were]</char> left. And Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> fled, and came into the city, into an inner chamber.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />And his servants said unto him, Behold now, we have heard that the kings of the house of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God] [are]</char> merciful kings: let us, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, put sackcloth on our waist, and ropes upon our heads, and go out to the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>: perhaps he will save your<char style="ord">i</char> life.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />So they girded sackcloth on their waist, and <char style="add">[put]</char> ropes on their heads, and came to the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, and said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> servant Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> says, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, let me live. And he said, <char style="add">[Is]</char> he still alive? he <char style="add">[is]</char> my brother.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />Now the men did diligently observe whether <char style="add">[anything would come]</char> from him, and did hastily catch <char style="add">[it]</char>: and they said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> brother Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char>. Then he said, Go you<char style="ord">2f</char>, bring him. Then Ben-Hadad <char style="add">[son of the (false god) Hadad]</char> came forth to him; and he caused him to come up into the chariot.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And <char style="add">[Ben-Hadad [son of the (false god) Hadad]]</char> said unto him, The cities, which my father took from your<char style="ord">i</char> father, I will restore; and you<char style="ord">i</char> shall make streets for you<char style="ord">i</char> in Dammesek <char style="pn">(Damascus)</char> <char style="add">[silent is the sackcloth weaver]</char>, as my father made in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>. Then <char style="add">[said Ach’av [father’s brother]]</char>, I will send you<char style="ord">i</char> away with this covenant. So he made a covenant with him, and sent him away.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And a certain man of the sons of the prophets said unto his neighbour in the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Strike me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>. And the man refused to strike him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />Then said he unto him, Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have not obeyed the voice of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, behold, as soon as you<char style="ord">i</char> are departed from me, a lion shall slay you<char style="ord">i</char>. And as soon as he was departed from him, a lion found him, and killed him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />Then he found another man, and said, Strike me, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>. And the man struck him, so that in striking a blow he wounded <char style="add">[him]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />So the prophet departed, and waited for the king by the way, and disguised himself with bandages over his eyes.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />And as the king passed by, he cried unto the king: and he said, Your<char style="ord">1s</char> servant went out into the thick of the battle; and, behold, a man turned aside, and brought a man unto me, and said, Keep this man: if by any means he be missing, then shall your<char style="ord">i</char> life be for his life, or else you<char style="ord">i</char> shall pay a talent <char style="pn">(weight of money; weight; gift)</char> of silver.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />And as your<char style="ord">i</char> servant was busy here and there, he was gone. And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto him, So <char style="add">[shall]</char> your<char style="ord">i</char> judgment <char style="add">[be]</char>; yourself have decided <char style="add">[it]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And he hasted, and took the ashes away from his face; and the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> he discerned that he <char style="add">[was]</char> of the prophets.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />And he said unto him, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Because you<char style="ord">i</char> have let go out of <char style="add">[your<char style="ord">i</char>]</char> hand a man whom I appointed to utter destruction, therefore your<char style="ord">i</char> life shall go for his life, and your<char style="ord">i</char> people for his people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> went to his house heavy and displeased, and came to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And it came to pass after these things, <char style="add">[that]</char> Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> the Yizre’eli <char style="add">[God Sows]</char> had a vineyard, which <char style="add">[was]</char> in Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, right next to the palace of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> spoke unto Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char>, saying, Give me your<char style="ord">i</char> vineyard, that I may have it for a garden of herbs, because it <char style="add">[is]</char> near unto my house: and I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> for it a better vineyard than it; <char style="add">[or]</char>, if it seem good to you<char style="ord">i</char>, I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> the monetary value of it in money.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> said to Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, The LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> forbid it me, that I should give the inheritance of my fathers unto you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> came into his house heavy and displeased because of the word which Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> the Yizre’eli <char style="add">[God Sows]</char> had spoken to him: for he had said, I will not give you<char style="ord">i</char> the inheritance of my fathers. And he laid him down upon his bed, and turned away his face, and would eat no bread.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />But Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> his wife came to him, and said unto him, Why is your<char style="ord">i</char> spirit so sad, that you<char style="ord">i</char> eat no bread?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />And he said unto her, Because I spoke unto Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> the Yizre’eli <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, and said unto him, Give me your<char style="ord">i</char> vineyard for money; or else, if it please you<char style="ord">i</char>, I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[another]</char> vineyard for it: and he answered, I will not give you<char style="ord">i</char> my vineyard.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> his wife said unto him, Do you<char style="ord">i</char> now govern the kingdom of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>? arise, <char style="add">[and]</char> eat bread, and let your<char style="ord">i</char> heart be merry: I will give you<char style="ord">i</char> the vineyard of Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> the Yizre’eli <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />So she wrote letters in Ach’av’s <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> name, and sealed <char style="add">[them]</char> with his seal, and sent the letters unto the elders and to the nobles that <char style="add">[were]</char> in his city, dwelling with Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />And she wrote in the letters, saying, Proclaim a fast, and set Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> on high among the people:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And set two men, sons of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, before him, to bear witness against him, saying, you<char style="ord">i</char> did blaspheme God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> and the king. And <char style="add">[then]</char> carry him out, and stone him, that he may die.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And the men of his city, <char style="add">[even]</char> the elders and the nobles who were the inhabitants in his city, did as Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> had sent unto them, <char style="add">[and]</char> as it <char style="add">[was]</char> written in the letters which she had sent unto them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />They proclaimed a fast, and set Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> on high among the people.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And there came in two men, children of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char>, and sat before him: and the men of Belial <char style="add">[Worthless, Good for Nothing]</char> witnessed against him, <char style="add">[even]</char> against Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char>, in the presence of the people, saying, Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> did blaspheme God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> and the king. Then they carried him forth out of the city, and stoned him with stones, that he died.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />Then they sent to Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char>, saying, Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> is stoned, and is dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> heard that Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> was stoned, and was dead, that Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> said to Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, Arise, take possession of the vineyard of Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> the Yizre’eli <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, which he refused to give you<char style="ord">i</char> for money: for Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> is not alive, but dead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> heard that Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> was dead, that Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> rose up to go down to the vineyard of Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> the Yizre’eli <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>, to take possession of it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the Tishbi <char style="add">[captivity]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />Arise, go down to meet Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, which <char style="add">[is]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>: behold, <char style="add">[he is]</char> in the vineyard of Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char>, to which he is gone down to possess it.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak unto him, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, Have you<char style="ord">i</char> killed, and also taken possession? And you<char style="ord">i</char> shall speak unto him, saying, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, In the place where dogs licked the blood of Navot <char style="add">[fruits]</char> shall dogs lick your<char style="ord">i</char> blood, even yoursi.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> said to Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char>, Have you<char style="ord">i</char> found me, O my enemy? And he answered, I have found <char style="pn">[you<char style="ord">i</char>]</char>: because you<char style="ord">i</char> have sold yourself to work evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />Behold, I will bring evil upon you<char style="ord">i</char>, and will take away your<char style="ord">i</char> posterity, and will cut off from Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> him that pisses against the wall, and him that is shut up and left in Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And will make your<char style="ord">i</char> house like the house of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, and like the house of Ba’sha <char style="add">[wicked]</char> the son of Achiyah <char style="add">[brother of Yehovah]</char>, for the provocation with which you<char style="ord">i</char> have provoked <char style="add">[me]</char> to anger, and made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />And of Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> also spoke the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, saying, The dogs shall eat Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> by the wall of Yizre’el <char style="add">[God Sows]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />Him that dies of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> in the city the dogs shall eat; and him that dies in the field shall the fowls of the air eat.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />But there was none like unto Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, which did sell himself to work wickedness in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, whom Izevel <char style="add">[Ba’al exalts]</char> his wife stirred up.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And he did very abominably in following idols, according to all <char style="add">[things]</char> as did the Emori <char style="add">[Highlanders]</char>, whom the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> cast out before the people of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And it came to pass, when Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> heard those words, that he rent his clothes, and put sackcloth upon his flesh, and fasted, and lay in sackcloth, and went softly.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> came to Eliyahu <char style="add">[my God is Yehovah]</char> the Tishbi <char style="add">[captivity]</char>, saying,</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />See you<char style="ord">i</char> how Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> humbles himself before me? because he humbles himself before me, I will not bring the evil in his days: <char style="add">[but]</char> in his son’s days will I bring the evil upon his house.</para>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" />
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" />And they continued three years without war between Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> and Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="2" style="v" />And it came to pass in the third year, that Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> came down to the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="3" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto his servants, Know you<char style="ord">2f</char> that Ramot <char style="add">[Heights]</char> in Gil’ad <char style="add">[Rocky Region] [is]</char> ours, and we do nothing to take it not out of the hand of the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" />And he said unto Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, Will you<char style="ord">i</char> go with me to battle to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>? And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said to the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, I <char style="add">[am]</char> as you<char style="ord">i</char> <char style="add">[are]</char>, my people as your<char style="ord">i</char> people, my horses as your<char style="ord">i</char> horses.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="5" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said unto the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, Enquire, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, at the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> today.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="6" style="v" />Then the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> gathered the prophets together, about four hundred men, and said unto them, Shall I go against Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char> to battle, or shall I refrain (restrain; refrein from acting)? And they said, Go up; for the Lord-Adonai <char style="pn">(The Father)</char> <char style="add">[Greatest Above All Things]</char> shall deliver <char style="add">[it]</char> into the hand of the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said, <char style="add">[Is there]</char> not here a prophet of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> besides, that we might enquire of him?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="8" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, <char style="add">[There is]</char> yet one man, Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> the son of Yimlah <char style="add">[whom God will fill up]</char>, by whom we may enquire of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: but I hate him; for he does not prophesy good concerning me, but evil. And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> said, The king shouldn’t say such a thing.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" />Then the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> called an officer, and said, Quickly bring <char style="add">[here]</char> Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> the son of Yimlah <char style="add">[whom God will fill up]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="10" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> sat each on his throne, having put on their robes, in an open place in the entrance of the gate of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>; and all the prophets prophesied before them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="11" style="v" />And Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char> the son of Kena’anah <char style="add">[trader]</char> made him horns of iron: and he said, Thus says the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, With these shall you<char style="ord">i</char> push the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>, until you<char style="ord">i</char> have consumed them.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" />And all the prophets prophesied so, saying, Go up to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>, and prosper: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall deliver <char style="add">[it]</char> into the king’s hand.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="13" style="v" />And the messenger that was gone to call Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> spoke unto him, saying, Behold now, the words of the prophets <char style="add">[declare]</char> good unto the king with one mouth: let your<char style="ord">i</char> word, I pray you<char style="ord">i</char>, be like the word of one of them, and speak <char style="add">[that which is]</char> good.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="14" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> said, <char style="add">[As]</char> the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> lives, what the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> says unto me, that will I speak.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="15" style="v" />So he came to the king. And the king said unto him, Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, shall we go against Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char> to battle, or shall we hold off? And he answered him, Go, and prosper: for the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> shall deliver <char style="add">[it]</char> into the hand of the king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="16" style="v" />And the king said unto him, How many times shall I adjure <char style="pn">(to command under oath or threat)</char> you<char style="ord">i</char> that you<char style="ord">i</char> tell me nothing but <char style="add">[that which is]</char> true in the name of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="17" style="v" />And he said, I saw all Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> scattered upon the hills, as sheep that have not a shepherd: and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, These have no master: let them return every man to his house in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="18" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, Did I not tell you<char style="ord">i</char> that he would prophesy no good concerning me, but evil?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="19" style="v" />And he said, Hear you<char style="ord">i</char> therefore the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: I saw the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> sitting on his throne, and all the army of heaven standing by him on his right hand and on his left.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="20" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said, Who shall persuade Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, that he may go up and fall at Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>? And one said do it this way, and another said do it this way.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="21" style="v" />And there came forth a spirit, and stood before the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and said, I will persuade <char style="pn">(entice)</char> him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="22" style="v" />And the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> said unto him, How? And he said, I will go forth, and I will be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets. And He said, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall persuade <char style="add">[him]</char>, and prevail also: go forth, and do so.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="23" style="v" />Now therefore, behold, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has put a lying spirit in the mouth of all these your<char style="ord">i</char> prophets, and the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has spoken evil concerning you<char style="ord">i</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="24" style="v" />But Tzidkiyah <char style="add">[Yehovah is righteous]</char> the son of Kena’anah <char style="add">[trader]</char> went near, and struck Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> on the cheek, and said, Which way went the Spirit of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> from me to speak to you<char style="ord">i</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="25" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> said, Behold, you<char style="ord">i</char> shall find out in that day, when you<char style="ord">i</char> shall go into an inner chamber to hide yourself.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="26" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said, Take Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char>, and carry him back unto ‘Amon <char style="add">[master workman]</char> the governor of the city, and to Yo’ash <char style="add">[Given by the Lord]</char> the king’s son;</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="27" style="v" />And say, Thus says the king, Put this <char style="add">[fellow]</char> in the prison, and feed him with bread of affliction and with water of affliction, until I come in peace.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="28" style="v" />And Mikhay’hu <char style="add">[who is like God?]</char> said, If you<char style="ord">i</char> return at all in peace, the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> has not spoken by me. And he said, Listen, O people, everyone of you.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="29" style="v" />So the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> went up to Ramot-Gil’ad <char style="add">[rocky region]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="30" style="v" />And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> said unto Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, I will disguise myself, and enter into the battle; but put you<char style="ord">i</char> on your<char style="ord">i</char> robes. And the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> disguised himself, and went into the battle.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="31" style="v" />But the king of Aram <char style="pn">(Syria)</char> <char style="add">[exalted]</char> commanded his thirty and two captains that had rule over his chariots, saying, Fight neither with small nor great, save only with the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="32" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the captains of the chariots saw Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, that they said, Surely it <char style="add">[is]</char> the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>. And they turned aside to fight against him: and Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> cried out.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="33" style="v" />And it came to pass, when the captains of the chariots perceived that it <char style="add">[was]</char> not the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, that they turned back from pursuing him.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="34" style="v" />And a <char style="add">[certain]</char> man drew a bow at random, and struck the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> between the joints of the harness: wherefore he said unto the driver of his chariot, Turn your<char style="ord">i</char> hand, and carry me out of the host; for I am wounded.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="35" style="v" />And the battle increased that day: and the king was detained <char style="pn">(held)</char> up in his chariot facing the Aram <char style="add">[Syrians]</char>, and died at even: and the blood ran out of the wound into the midst of the chariot.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="36" style="v" />And there went a proclamation throughout the host about the going down of the sun, saying, Every man to his city, and every man to his own country.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="37" style="v" />So the king died, and was brought to Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>; and they buried the king in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="38" style="v" />And <char style="add">[one]</char> washed the chariot in the pool of Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char>; and the dogs licked up his blood; and they washed his armour; according unto the word of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> which he spoke.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="39" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char>, and all that he did, and the ivory house which he made, and all the cities that he built, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="40" style="v" />So Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> slept with his fathers; and Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="41" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> the son of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> began to reign over Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char> in the fourth year of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="42" style="v" />Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged] [was]</char> thirty and five years old when he began to reign; and he reigned twenty and five years in Yerushalayim <char style="add">[Foundation of Peace]</char>. And his mother’s name <char style="add">[was]</char> ‘Azuvah <char style="add">[forsaken]</char> the daughter of Shilchi <char style="add">[armed]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="43" style="v" />And he walked in all the ways of Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char> his father; he turned not aside from it, doing <char style="add">[that which was]</char> right in the eyes of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>: nevertheless the high places were not taken away; <char style="add">[for]</char> the people offered and burnt incense yet in the high places.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="44" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> made peace with the king of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="45" style="v" />Now the rest of the acts of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, and his might that he showed, and how he warred, <char style="add">[are]</char> they not written in the book of the Chronicles of the Kings of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>?</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="46" style="v" />And the remnant of the sodomites, which remained in the days of his father Asa <char style="add">[healer; injurious?]</char>, he took out of the land.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="47" style="v" />
    <char style="add">[There was]</char> then no king in Edom <char style="add">[Red]</char>: a deputy <char style="add">[was]</char> king.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="48" style="v" />Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> made ships of Tarshish <char style="add">[yellow jasper]</char> to go to Ofir <char style="add">[reducing to ashes]</char> for gold: but they went not; for the ships were broken at ‘Etzyon-Gever <char style="add">[backbone of a man]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="49" style="v" />Then said Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> unto Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char>, Let my servants go with your<char style="ord">i</char> servants in the ships. But Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> would not.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="50" style="v" />And Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> slept with his fathers, and was buried with his fathers in the city of David <char style="add">[beloved]</char> his father: and Y’horam <char style="add">[Yehovah is exalted]</char> his son reigned in his stead.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="51" style="v" />Achazyah <char style="add">[Yehovah possesses]</char> the son of Ach’av <char style="add">[father’s brother]</char> began to reign over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> in Shomron <char style="add">[watch mountain]</char> the seventeenth year of Y’hoshafat <char style="add">[Yehovah has judged]</char> king of Y’hudah <char style="add">[Let Him (God) Be Praised]</char>, and reigned two years over Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>.</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="52" style="v" />And he did evil in the sight of the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char>, and walked in the way of his father, and in the way of his mother, and in the way of Yarov’am <char style="add">[the people will contend]</char> the son of N’vat <char style="add">[aspect]</char>, who made Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char> to sin:</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="53" style="v" />For he served Ba’al <char style="add">[lord (a false god)]</char>, and worshipped him, and provoked to anger the LORD-Yehōvah <char style="pn">(Messiah Pre-Incarnate)</char> God-Elōhīm <char style="pn">(The Living Word)</char> <char style="add">[The Many Powered]</char> of Yisra’el <char style="add">[He Holds Onto The Heel Of God]</char>, according to all that his father had done.</para>
</usx>